Her golden Valna medallion.

271
00:08:22,819 --> 00:08:24,579
- Which Ken hocked for
a pack of cigarettes.

272
00:08:24,579 --> 00:08:26,459
- [Voiceover] Ken will never forget her.

273
00:08:26,459 --> 00:08:29,376
- Or the VISA bill she ran up, huh?

274
00:08:30,219 --> 00:08:31,579
- Oh it's over, then.

275
00:08:31,579 --> 00:08:32,981
- Amen.

276
00:08:32,981 --> 00:08:34,597
- Is it ay-men or ah-men?

277
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:35,785
- [Voiceover] Now Ken
and his Earth comrades

278
00:08:35,785 --> 00:08:37,465
are off in quest of new adventure.

279
00:08:37,465 --> 00:08:38,985
Their mission to fly to Saysar,

280
00:08:38,985 --> 00:08:41,105
find a secret weapon and destroy it.

281
00:08:41,105 --> 00:08:42,425
- And hopefully do a little shopping.

282
00:08:42,425 --> 00:08:44,465
- Let's take a look at that wound, Ken.

283
00:08:44,465 --> 00:08:46,865
Oh good, it's healing beautifully.

284
00:08:46,865 --> 00:08:47,698
Okay?

285
00:08:49,625 --> 00:08:50,538
I'm finished.

286
00:08:50,538 --> 00:08:51,371
- I remember this.

287
00:08:51,371 --> 00:08:52,204
(sings)

288
00:08:52,204 --> 00:08:53,097
♫ I love Ken, he is my friend,

289
00:08:53,097 --> 00:08:54,495
♫ I love Ken, he is my sweet friend ♫

290
00:08:54,495 --> 00:08:56,615
- Well, I must say, you're
a real angel of mercy.

291
00:08:56,615 --> 00:08:58,695
You never fuss like this when I get hurt,

292
00:08:58,695 --> 00:09:00,855
you always tell me, "Bear it like a man."

293
00:09:00,855 --> 00:09:02,455
- Oh come on Dan, your
problem is you're jealous.

294
00:09:02,455 --> 00:09:04,015
(laughs)

295
00:09:04,015 --> 00:09:05,015
- Quit teasing.

296
00:09:05,015 --> 00:09:05,848
- Okay.

297
00:09:05,848 --> 00:09:06,765
- Terrific.

298
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,071
- Dan, just keep your eye on the course.

299
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:12,349
I don't trust (mumbles)

300
00:09:12,349 --> 00:09:14,469
There's something peculiar about him.

301
00:09:14,469 --> 00:09:15,389
- Mmm hmm!

302
00:09:15,389 --> 00:09:17,049
That's good blow, mmm hmm!

303
00:09:17,049 --> 00:09:17,885
- [Voiceover] I've heard
you're one of Saysar's

304
00:09:17,885 --> 00:09:19,845
top experts in advanced
defense technology.

305
00:09:19,845 --> 00:09:21,085
- You heard right.

306
00:09:21,085 --> 00:09:22,885
- [Voiceover] Then you
probably know all about

307
00:09:22,885 --> 00:09:25,285
that secret weapon Saysar
is said to have imported

308
00:09:25,285 --> 00:09:26,767
from another planet.

309
00:09:26,767 --> 00:09:28,447
- Pretty much.

310
00:09:28,447 --> 00:09:29,927
- Are there any truth to those rumors?

311
00:09:29,927 --> 00:09:31,127
Colonel?

312
00:09:31,127 --> 00:09:32,609
- They say it could blow up the universe.

313
00:09:32,609 --> 00:09:33,809
- Or worse!

314
00:09:33,809 --> 00:09:34,649
- Where did you hear that?

315
00:09:34,649 --> 00:09:36,069
(chuckles)

316
00:09:36,069 --> 00:09:37,709
- You know, occasionally I tune into

317
00:09:37,709 --> 00:09:39,149
the intergalactic grapevine.

318
00:09:39,149 --> 00:09:40,869
(chuckles)

319
00:09:40,869 --> 00:09:42,309
- Joe, shut up.

320
00:09:42,309 --> 00:09:45,669
I take it you're trying
to enlist my cooperation

321
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:47,429
for a mission you're about to undertake.

322
00:09:47,429 --> 00:09:48,951
(groans)

323
00:09:48,951 --> 00:09:52,233
Before I say yes or no, I'll need to know

324
00:09:52,233 --> 00:09:53,753
a bit more about your intentions.

325
00:09:53,753 --> 00:09:55,313
- I'll love you all the days of my life.

326
00:09:55,313 --> 00:09:57,033
- I don't know what ever gave you the idea

327
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:59,593
we're planning a mission,
we're just out for a ride.

328
00:09:59,593 --> 00:10:01,793
A little excursion to discover more facts

329
00:10:01,793 --> 00:10:03,113
about our universe.

330
00:10:03,113 --> 00:10:04,113
(laughs)

331
00:10:04,113 --> 00:10:05,353
- You don't say?

332
00:10:05,353 --> 00:10:07,073
And how do I know I can trust you?

333
00:10:07,073 --> 00:10:10,073
This Ken fellow seems
mighty suspicious to me.

334
00:10:10,073 --> 00:10:12,153
- Ken's just a bit of a loner.

335
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:14,273
If you want I'll call him in

336
00:10:14,273 --> 00:10:15,713
and you can talk to him yourself.

337
00:10:15,713 --> 00:10:16,713
- Ken's a loaner?

338
00:10:16,713 --> 00:10:18,793
How long before your Ken is fixed?

339
00:10:18,793 --> 00:10:19,876
- Ken? Tammy?

340
00:10:20,713 --> 00:10:22,833
I wanna see you.

341
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:23,835
- Oh great.

342
00:10:23,835 --> 00:10:25,677
He found out about the keg!

343
00:10:25,677 --> 00:10:26,517
(dramatic sound)

344
00:10:26,517 --> 00:10:28,119
- Plot point, right there.

345
00:10:28,119 --> 00:10:29,279
- Hmm?

346
00:10:29,279 --> 00:10:31,239
- This is a girl officer's insignia.

347
00:10:31,239 --> 00:10:32,919
How did you get it?

348
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:35,639
- A lotta hard work and
a lotta pancake makeup.

349
00:10:35,639 --> 00:10:38,239
- When you were sleeping,
I heard you call out

350
00:10:38,239 --> 00:10:39,439
a girl's name out loud.

351
00:10:39,439 --> 00:10:40,799
- But when I put your hand in warm water--

352
00:10:40,799 --> 00:10:42,639
- Rita, I think.

353
00:10:42,639 --> 00:10:44,239
I believe that was it.

354
00:10:44,239 --> 00:10:46,159
Does the name Rita mean anything to you?

355
00:10:46,159 --> 00:10:48,079
- Uh, it's a Beatles song.

356
00:10:48,079 --> 00:10:48,912
- Ken!

357
00:10:50,199 --> 00:10:51,519
- [Voiceover] This is
our present position.

358
00:10:51,519 --> 00:10:53,959
Pegasus R-2, bias four, right here.

359
00:10:53,959 --> 00:10:56,461
- Here's the Spencer gifts.

360
00:10:56,461 --> 00:10:58,221
- Distance to Saysar is a roller time.

361
00:10:58,221 --> 00:10:59,054
- A rolla-huh?

362
00:10:59,054 --> 00:11:00,301
- A Roladex.

363
00:11:00,301 --> 00:11:02,461
- Two one, three, sir.

364
00:11:02,461 --> 00:11:04,501
- Course three seven is perfectly safe.

365
00:11:04,501 --> 00:11:06,301
It's when we switch to course T

366
00:11:06,301 --> 00:11:08,661
that we're likely to run into trouble.

367
00:11:08,661 --> 00:11:11,021
There's a huge black
hole near R-5 by nine.

368
00:11:11,021 --> 00:11:12,221
I don't know any way we
can navigate around it.

369
00:11:12,221 --> 00:11:13,141
- A vicious dog leg to the left.

370
00:11:13,141 --> 00:11:14,641
- Black hole, huh?

371
00:11:16,497 --> 00:11:18,777
It swallows up anything
that comes near it.

372
00:11:18,777 --> 00:11:19,697
(scratching sound)

373
00:11:19,697 --> 00:11:21,337
I don't think we can risk it.

374
00:11:21,337 --> 00:11:23,057
(dramatic music)

375
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,937
- Artwork and other
paintings by Judy Chicago,

376
00:11:24,937 --> 00:11:26,417
now back to our movie.

377
00:11:26,417 --> 00:11:28,577
- This puts a new light on
the conditions of our mission.

378
00:11:28,577 --> 00:11:30,021
- A black light.

379
00:11:30,021 --> 00:11:32,017
- Our odds against success
are extremely high.

380
00:11:32,017 --> 00:11:34,257
- Well then, I'm extremely high.

381
00:11:34,257 --> 00:11:35,857
- On the other hand, if you gotta go,

382
00:11:35,857 --> 00:11:37,177
I can't think of a better way.

383
00:11:37,177 --> 00:11:38,777
- That's not funny, sir.

384
00:11:38,777 --> 00:11:40,019
- I'll say it isn't.

385
00:11:40,019 --> 00:11:41,977
I don't wanna vanish in thin air.

386
00:11:41,977 --> 00:11:44,857
When my time comes, I
wanna go out in glory.

387
00:11:44,857 --> 00:11:46,297
- I wanna be torn apart by animals!

388
00:11:46,297 --> 00:11:47,457
- Spoken like a true woman.

389
00:11:47,457 --> 00:11:48,579
And a naive one.

390
00:11:48,579 --> 00:11:49,579
- Naive yourself!

391
00:11:49,579 --> 00:11:50,579
- Me so silly.

392
00:11:50,579 --> 00:11:51,699
(laughs)

393
00:11:51,699 --> 00:11:53,619
- Captain Joe, you don't
necessarily have to

394
00:11:53,619 --> 00:11:54,819
get swallowed up in a black hole.

395
00:11:54,819 --> 00:11:56,099
- But it helps.

396
00:11:56,099 --> 00:11:57,899
- If you chart your course carefully.

397
00:11:57,899 --> 00:11:58,899
You can go through a tunnel out

398
00:11:58,899 --> 00:12:01,849
to a white hole and safety.

399
00:12:01,849 --> 00:12:03,578
It's a tricky maneuver.

400
00:12:03,578 --> 00:12:05,774
- Where did you hear that?

401
00:12:05,774 --> 00:12:07,094
- Where did I hear it?

402
00:12:07,094 --> 00:12:08,654
I'm afraid I don't remember.

403
00:12:08,654 --> 00:12:10,454
I guess it was at one of
those scientific briefings

404
00:12:10,454 --> 00:12:11,454
I attended.

405
00:12:11,454 --> 00:12:13,094
- Yeah, at my aunt's house or something.

406
00:12:13,094 --> 00:12:13,927
- Yeah.

407
00:12:17,296 --> 00:12:18,354
- Ken, wait!

408
00:12:18,354 --> 00:12:19,634
You're walking down someone's throat!

409
00:12:19,634 --> 00:12:21,274
(chuckles)

410
00:12:21,274 --> 00:12:23,114
- Wait a second, I didn't
tell you the punchline.

411
00:12:23,114 --> 00:12:24,876
- Slip of the tongue and you
gave your whole game away,

412
00:12:24,876 --> 00:12:25,793
didn't you?

413
00:12:26,716 --> 00:12:28,318
- I don't understand.

414
00:12:28,318 --> 00:12:29,878
- Do you find me pleasing?

415
00:12:29,878 --> 00:12:31,680
- I know for a fact that only a handful

416
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,600
of Wolf attackers have
ever made it through

417
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:37,040
a black hole and still
lived to tell the tale.

418
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:38,840
I only have to put two and
two together to realize

419
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,200
you're a Star Wolf.

420
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,200
(grunting)

421
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:42,680
- Who are you to judge?

422
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,960
- Don't be a fool Ken, I'm the only friend

423
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,680
you've got here!

424
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,480
(grunts)

425
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:50,200
(coughs)

426
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,200
- What's up?

427
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,640
What's going on?

428
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,307
- It's all my fault.

429
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:58,160
- He was just showing
him where his larynx was.

430
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:01,000
- I foolishly made a sarcastic
remark about earthlings.

431
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,362
Ken was right to act as he did.

432
00:13:04,362 --> 00:13:06,802
Ill-chosen words have
been known to start wars.

433
00:13:06,802 --> 00:13:08,724
- Yeah, like the sarcasm wars of 1999.

434
00:13:08,724 --> 00:13:09,804
(chuckles)

435
00:13:09,804 --> 00:13:11,137
What a dipstick.

436
00:13:12,964 --> 00:13:15,204
- I don't like that guy.

437
00:13:15,204 --> 00:13:17,084
And I don't like you, either.

438
00:13:17,084 --> 00:13:18,284
- The feeling is mutual, Rocky.

439
00:13:18,284 --> 00:13:19,964
- Oh Rocky, who do you like?

440
00:13:19,964 --> 00:13:21,084
- [Man] Captain!

441
00:13:21,084 --> 00:13:22,751
Come up here, quick!

442
00:13:23,684 --> 00:13:24,684
- Surprise!

443
00:13:24,684 --> 00:13:26,124
Happy Birthday to you!

444
00:13:26,124 --> 00:13:27,204
- Look at that, sir.

445
00:13:27,204 --> 00:13:28,524
What do you make of it?

446
00:13:28,524 --> 00:13:30,124
- Ah, it's one of those nut clusters!

447
00:13:30,124 --> 00:13:31,484
- Looks like a meteorite.

448
00:13:31,484 --> 00:13:32,764
Quite a big one.

449
00:13:32,764 --> 00:13:33,764
- Yeah, just one thing's wrong,

450
00:13:33,764 --> 00:13:35,806
I don't see it on any chart.

451
00:13:35,806 --> 00:13:37,086
- Well the time they get it on the chart

452
00:13:37,086 --> 00:13:38,246
it'll probably have broken up.

453
00:13:38,246 --> 00:13:39,646
- Like most rock bands.

454
00:13:39,646 --> 00:13:40,479
- Oh that's a good one.

455
00:13:40,479 --> 00:13:41,312
(laughs)

456
00:13:41,312 --> 00:13:42,145
- Do I speak the truth?

457
00:13:42,145 --> 00:13:42,978
- You bet.

458
00:13:42,978 --> 00:13:43,811
- Amen.

459
00:13:43,811 --> 00:13:44,974
- Looks like we're getting
into hostile territory.

460
00:13:44,974 --> 00:13:46,696
We have to be on our guard.

461
00:13:46,696 --> 00:13:47,816
Rocky, take the controls.

462
00:13:47,816 --> 00:13:48,936
- Again?

463
00:13:48,936 --> 00:13:50,336
- Kelly, back to your station.

464
00:13:50,336 --> 00:13:51,456
- Yes sir.

465
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:52,289
- Rocky, you hate Ken.

466
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,122
Ken, you make goofy faces.

467
00:13:53,122 --> 00:13:53,955
- Tammy, you love Rocky.

468
00:13:53,955 --> 00:13:55,096
Or Ken.

469
00:13:55,096 --> 00:13:56,136
- Colonel, you're ruling.

470
00:13:56,136 --> 00:13:57,376
- That's your seat there.

471
00:13:57,376 --> 00:13:58,256
- But Captain--

472
00:13:58,256 --> 00:13:59,296
- He said, sit down.

473
00:13:59,296 --> 00:14:00,816
- But he didn't say Simon Says!

474
00:14:00,816 --> 00:14:02,296
- He said, "Captain says."

475
00:14:02,296 --> 00:14:03,296
- Oh wait a minute.

476
00:14:03,296 --> 00:14:04,936
Which is moving, the stars or the ship?

477
00:14:04,936 --> 00:14:06,696
- Mmm, stars?

478
00:14:06,696 --> 00:14:08,456
- Pink Floyd on the headphones,

479
00:14:08,456 --> 00:14:12,096
set the controls for Heart of the Sun.

480
00:14:12,096 --> 00:14:13,216
- It's broccoli!

481
00:14:13,216 --> 00:14:15,298
I hate broccoli.

482
00:14:15,298 --> 00:14:18,020
- You know, he's got
Kristy McNichol cheeks.

483
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:20,270
- I don't like this at all.

484
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,420
Ken!

485
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:23,253
- Yes sir?

486
00:14:23,253 --> 00:14:25,000
- Destroy the meteorite
with the folic laser.

487
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,280
- Okay, yes sir.

488
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,720
(shoots)

489
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,720
(sings together)

490
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,960
♫ Love, love, love ♫

491
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,460
(techy music)

492
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:37,680
- Captain Joe, we're still alive.

493
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,880
That's the only thing that counts.

494
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:39,880
- No it isn't.

495
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,040
- No, cleanliness is the
only thing that counts.

496
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:43,562
- I wouldn't feel safe while he's alive.

497
00:14:43,562 --> 00:14:44,802
- Kill him!

498
00:14:44,802 --> 00:14:45,882
- [Voiceover] What do
you think you're doing?

499
00:14:45,882 --> 00:14:47,242
- We've got a mission to accomplish.

500
00:14:47,242 --> 00:14:48,682
I'm just gonna remove an obstacle.

501
00:14:48,682 --> 00:14:50,442
- Your eyebrow.

502
00:14:50,442 --> 00:14:51,682
- Ken, stop him!

503
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:53,282
If he kills me, you're next!

504
00:14:53,282 --> 00:14:54,922
- Easy, Rocky.

505
00:14:54,922 --> 00:14:56,042
This isn't the right moment.

506
00:14:56,042 --> 00:14:57,082
- Outta my way.

507
00:14:57,082 --> 00:14:58,122
- Rocky, hold your fire.

508
00:14:58,122 --> 00:14:59,162
- Again?

509
00:14:59,162 --> 00:15:00,762
- I'm sorry to say, we still need him.

510
00:15:00,762 --> 00:15:02,202
- Need him for what?

511
00:15:02,202 --> 00:15:04,282
- We rescued him to guide us
to Saysar, and he'll do it.

512
00:15:04,282 --> 00:15:05,564
Lock him up.

513
00:15:05,564 --> 00:15:06,397
- Rocko!

514
00:15:07,324 --> 00:15:08,364
- Whatever you say.

515
00:15:08,364 --> 00:15:10,204
I just hope you know what you're doing.

516
00:15:10,204 --> 00:15:12,004
- I just wanna say your makeup sucks.

517
00:15:12,004 --> 00:15:13,684
(suspenseful music)

518
00:15:13,684 --> 00:15:15,166
- As long as this guy
is traveling with us,

519
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:16,566
our mission is threatened.

520
00:15:16,566 --> 00:15:18,486
- We'll never make it to Woodstock!

521
00:15:18,486 --> 00:15:20,286
- Huh? Huh? Huh?

522
00:15:20,286 --> 00:15:21,619
Huh? Who? Wha--?

523
00:15:23,086 --> 00:15:26,849
(continuous uttering)

524
00:15:26,849 --> 00:15:28,932
(growls)

525
00:15:32,328 --> 00:15:34,488
- Well here you are, this
isn't the royal suite,

526
00:15:34,488 --> 00:15:36,208
but it'll just have to do.

527
00:15:36,208 --> 00:15:37,688
- You want room service, dial nine.

528
00:15:37,688 --> 00:15:39,128
There's a mint on the pillow.

529
00:15:39,128 --> 00:15:40,328
- I need some towels!

530
00:15:40,328 --> 00:15:41,770
- Listen to me!

531
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:43,090
You wanna make it to Saysar in one piece,

532
00:15:43,090 --> 00:15:45,052
you need me to guide you.

533
00:15:45,052 --> 00:15:46,972
Any minute now we'll be
going by Demetor Star.

534
00:15:46,972 --> 00:15:48,692
It'll set us on fire!

535
00:15:48,692 --> 00:15:49,972
Let me out!

536
00:15:49,972 --> 00:15:51,532
Let me out!

537
00:15:51,532 --> 00:15:52,812
- I'm gonna hold my
breath until I turn blue!

538
00:15:52,812 --> 00:15:53,812
Oh, I'm already.

539
00:15:53,812 --> 00:15:55,092
Oh, I did it again.

540
00:15:55,092 --> 00:15:56,412
I'm already blue!

