Oh! He's a good--

820
00:23:35,304 --> 00:23:36,304
Oh!

821
00:23:36,304 --> 00:23:37,824
- Crow, you listen to
me and you listen good,

822
00:23:37,824 --> 00:23:39,384
I need you to snap out of Shatner,

823
00:23:39,384 --> 00:23:42,224
I need you hear now, our friend's
life hangs in the balance!

824
00:23:42,224 --> 00:23:43,226
(sobs)

825
00:23:43,226 --> 00:23:44,824
- I'm sorry, I don't even--

826
00:23:44,824 --> 00:23:46,104
(sobs)

827
00:23:46,104 --> 00:23:47,544
- I know man, I know.

828
00:23:47,544 --> 00:23:49,544
But we gotta get our little buddy

829
00:23:49,544 --> 00:23:51,184
out of the bone orchard, okay?

830
00:23:51,184 --> 00:23:53,384
Listen, I need you to run along

831
00:23:53,384 --> 00:23:55,226
and get the defibrillator
and I'm gonna try

832
00:23:55,226 --> 00:23:57,626
to get our brother Tommy
out of the Badlands.

833
00:23:57,626 --> 00:23:58,626
- [Crow] Alright, alright.

834
00:23:58,626 --> 00:23:59,986
- Come on, man.

835
00:23:59,986 --> 00:24:01,786
Come on back, we're all
pulling for you, buddy.

836
00:24:01,786 --> 00:24:03,586
(sobs)

837
00:24:03,586 --> 00:24:05,546
- [Crow] Hey Joel, is the
defibrillator the thing

838
00:24:05,546 --> 00:24:07,066
that looks like a vacuum cleaner

839
00:24:07,066 --> 00:24:09,226
or a thing that looks
like a battery charger?

840
00:24:09,226 --> 00:24:11,226
- It's the thing that looks like

841
00:24:11,226 --> 00:24:13,666
a battery charger, now would
you get it together man

842
00:24:13,666 --> 00:24:14,499
and get out here?

843
00:24:14,499 --> 00:24:15,380
I mean it's Tom Servo's life!

844
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:17,340
Hang on, buddy!

845
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:18,500
(grunts)

846
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:20,062
Okay, hold on buddy, it's coming!

847
00:24:20,062 --> 00:24:21,062
Come on Tom!

848
00:24:22,462 --> 00:24:24,382
Come on back, buddy!

849
00:24:24,382 --> 00:24:25,822
Clear!

850
00:24:25,822 --> 00:24:29,214
(buzzing sound)

851
00:24:29,214 --> 00:24:30,382
Nothing!

852
00:24:30,382 --> 00:24:31,622
Clear!

853
00:24:31,622 --> 00:24:34,182
(buzzing)

854
00:24:34,182 --> 00:24:35,262
He's coming back!

855
00:24:35,262 --> 00:24:36,422
He's coming back!

856
00:24:36,422 --> 00:24:38,182
- Come on, Tommy!

857
00:24:38,182 --> 00:24:40,102
(coughs)

858
00:24:40,102 --> 00:24:41,102
(grunts)

859
00:24:41,102 --> 00:24:42,182
- Oh, oh, oh!

860
00:24:42,182 --> 00:24:43,542
So I'm dancing up to the plate now,

861
00:24:43,542 --> 00:24:44,662
and, beautiful day here at Wrigley Field,

862
00:24:44,662 --> 00:24:46,862
boy, let me tell ya, perfect
for a nice cold Budweiser.

863
00:24:46,862 --> 00:24:48,342
You know, Lincoln carpeting--

864
00:24:48,342 --> 00:24:51,064
(coughs)

865
00:24:51,064 --> 00:24:51,981
Joel, Crow.

866
00:24:53,064 --> 00:24:54,384
What the heck happened to me?

867
00:24:54,384 --> 00:24:56,264
- It's okay buddy, you're
among the living now.

868
00:24:56,264 --> 00:24:57,264
(sighs)

869
00:24:57,264 --> 00:24:58,304
- That was weird.

870
00:24:58,304 --> 00:25:00,744
I was walking down a long hallway,

871
00:25:00,744 --> 00:25:03,104
and at the end of it was a bright light.

872
00:25:03,104 --> 00:25:04,864
And a kind man with a
beard reaching his hand

873
00:25:04,864 --> 00:25:06,384
out to me, beckoning me.

874
00:25:06,384 --> 00:25:09,224
And he looked at me so I got closer,

875
00:25:09,224 --> 00:25:11,944
and he said, "Hey buddy,
can you spare some change?"

876
00:25:11,944 --> 00:25:12,944
"I wanna cup of coffee!"

877
00:25:12,944 --> 00:25:13,924
(laughs)

878
00:25:13,924 --> 00:25:15,124
- Everything's a joke to you.

879
00:25:15,124 --> 00:25:16,444
That's great.

880
00:25:16,444 --> 00:25:17,484
We got commercials.

881
00:25:17,484 --> 00:25:18,724
- We should have let you die.

882
00:25:18,724 --> 00:25:20,164
- Ah, life.

883
00:25:20,164 --> 00:25:22,664
(techy music)

884
00:25:27,370 --> 00:25:29,210
You guys just have no sense of humor.

885
00:25:29,210 --> 00:25:30,810
Spoil sports.

886
00:25:30,810 --> 00:25:31,890
(muttering)

887
00:25:31,890 --> 00:25:33,010
- You have to check the Z system.

888
00:25:33,010 --> 00:25:34,090
Over here.

889
00:25:34,090 --> 00:25:34,923
- Alright.

890
00:25:39,010 --> 00:25:39,843
- Say!

891
00:25:42,295 --> 00:25:43,128
Oh.

892
00:25:45,002 --> 00:25:46,002
- Peeky-boo!

893
00:25:49,242 --> 00:25:51,159
- Okay, let's see here.

894
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:55,969
There it is, apartment 3B.

895
00:25:57,442 --> 00:25:59,609
(beeping)

896
00:26:02,642 --> 00:26:04,302
- What is this, The Super?

897
00:26:04,302 --> 00:26:05,542
(dramatic music)

898
00:26:05,542 --> 00:26:06,384
- Cheap Japanese crap!

899
00:26:06,384 --> 00:26:07,424
Look at that!

900
00:26:07,424 --> 00:26:09,257
- For crying out loud.

901
00:26:12,104 --> 00:26:13,706
- You know you wanna turn the power off

902
00:26:13,706 --> 00:26:14,986
before you work with something like that.

903
00:26:14,986 --> 00:26:17,106
- But he's in a rubber suit--

904
00:26:17,106 --> 00:26:19,856
(ringing sounds)

905
00:26:21,399 --> 00:26:22,346
- What?

906
00:26:22,346 --> 00:26:23,179
(groans)

907
00:26:23,179 --> 00:26:24,012
- Captain Joe?

908
00:26:24,012 --> 00:26:24,946
Ken here.

909
00:26:24,946 --> 00:26:25,946
- Ken.

910
00:26:25,946 --> 00:26:28,346
I can't hold out much longer.

911
00:26:28,346 --> 00:26:29,546
Hurry up.

912
00:26:29,546 --> 00:26:31,506
(groans)

913
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:33,268
- Woah, Linda Blair all of a sudden.

914
00:26:33,268 --> 00:26:34,668
- Are you alright?

915
00:26:34,668 --> 00:26:35,501
Captain?

916
00:26:38,548 --> 00:26:40,428
- Trying to kill me with a forklift.

917
00:26:40,428 --> 00:26:41,828
Ah, cheap Japanese crap. (mutters)

918
00:26:41,828 --> 00:26:42,661
What?

919
00:26:43,548 --> 00:26:44,548
- Yurulin here.

920
00:26:44,548 --> 00:26:45,828
What is it?

921
00:26:45,828 --> 00:26:47,228
- Colonel Yurulin.

922
00:26:47,228 --> 00:26:48,268
I'm worried about the Captain.

923
00:26:48,268 --> 00:26:49,548
Please check on him.

924
00:26:49,548 --> 00:26:50,548
- Alright.

925
00:26:50,548 --> 00:26:51,548
Right away.

926
00:26:51,548 --> 00:26:53,388
- I'm doing it, geez.

927
00:26:53,388 --> 00:26:54,388
(exhales)

928
00:26:54,388 --> 00:26:56,388
(pants)

929
00:27:01,982 --> 00:27:03,422
- You know apparently,
it's one of those things

930
00:27:03,422 --> 00:27:05,022
where if the tail light
goes out the whole thing

931
00:27:05,022 --> 00:27:06,022
shuts down?

932
00:27:06,022 --> 00:27:07,222
- Pretty much.

933
00:27:07,222 --> 00:27:10,142
- Oh, genie wants to
get outta there, look.

934
00:27:10,142 --> 00:27:12,392
(chuckles)

935
00:27:13,942 --> 00:27:15,782
Drink me, drink me.

936
00:27:15,782 --> 00:27:17,702
Come on and drink me.

937
00:27:17,702 --> 00:27:18,862
- Dr. Joe, is anything the matter?

938
00:27:18,862 --> 00:27:21,102
- Oh, I'm fine, just
reflecting on the Upanishads,

939
00:27:21,102 --> 00:27:21,935
young man--

940
00:27:21,935 --> 00:27:22,982
- What's wrong, Captain?

941
00:27:22,982 --> 00:27:24,022
Captain!

942
00:27:24,022 --> 00:27:25,022
(groans)

943
00:27:25,022 --> 00:27:26,022
I'd better take over the controls,

944
00:27:26,022 --> 00:27:27,142
you sit back there.

945
00:27:27,142 --> 00:27:30,544
- Yeah, you sleep, I'll
drive to Cleveland.

946
00:27:30,544 --> 00:27:33,104
- If it's not one thing it's
another in this crazy ship.

947
00:27:33,104 --> 00:27:34,868
For crying out loud.

948
00:27:34,868 --> 00:27:37,428
(eerie music)

949
00:27:37,428 --> 00:27:38,790
- Hey, turn off your brights.

950
00:27:38,790 --> 00:27:40,250
Dim it, dim the high beam!

951
00:27:40,250 --> 00:27:41,570
The high beams!

952
00:27:41,570 --> 00:27:43,690
- Ken, we're getting closer.

953
00:27:43,690 --> 00:27:46,170
Get that engine fixed right away!

954
00:27:46,170 --> 00:27:47,570
- [Voiceover] Now it's up to Ken.

955
00:27:47,570 --> 00:27:49,610
The fate of the entire
crew is in his hands.

956
00:27:49,610 --> 00:27:51,650
He will have to locate the short circuit.

957
00:27:51,650 --> 00:27:52,690
(vocalizes)

958
00:27:52,690 --> 00:27:54,570
Somewhere in the system
before the spacecraft

959
00:27:54,570 --> 00:27:56,690
gets closer to the exploding star.

960
00:27:56,690 --> 00:27:58,770
Otherwise, all is lost.

961
00:27:58,770 --> 00:27:59,930
- I knew vo-tech would pay off,

962
00:27:59,930 --> 00:28:01,450
I'm a graduate of DeVry!

963
00:28:01,450 --> 00:28:03,730
(pants)

964
00:28:03,730 --> 00:28:05,897
(beeping)

965
00:28:08,052 --> 00:28:09,752
- Alright, we can get free HBO now.

966
00:28:09,752 --> 00:28:10,752
(cheers)

967
00:28:10,752 --> 00:28:12,312
- Colonel, I fixed it.

968
00:28:12,312 --> 00:28:14,312
Start the engines, let's get going.

969
00:28:14,312 --> 00:28:15,472
- All right.

970
00:28:15,472 --> 00:28:17,472
- That was Ken.

971
00:28:17,472 --> 00:28:18,952
He's working late, he'll
be out for a while.

972
00:28:18,952 --> 00:28:20,952
We might was well go ahead and eat.

973
00:28:20,952 --> 00:28:25,119
- This is a really important
part of the film here.

974
00:28:26,432 --> 00:28:28,432
- Now, where are my keys?

975
00:28:28,432 --> 00:28:29,432
I left--

976
00:28:29,432 --> 00:28:31,515
(groans)

977
00:28:35,074 --> 00:28:36,272
- It isn't working.

978
00:28:36,272 --> 00:28:37,314
I can't make it start.

979
00:28:37,314 --> 00:28:38,314
That wasn't it.

980
00:28:38,314 --> 00:28:39,394
You'd better check it again.

981
00:28:39,394 --> 00:28:40,394
- [Ken] But Colonel!

982
00:28:40,394 --> 00:28:41,227
- Don't argue!

983
00:28:41,227 --> 00:28:42,627
- Pump it a few times!

984
00:28:42,627 --> 00:28:43,460
- I don't understand.

985
00:28:43,460 --> 00:28:44,426
It's gotta work.

986
00:28:44,426 --> 00:28:45,866
- Doggone it.

987
00:28:45,866 --> 00:28:48,746
(whistles)

988
00:28:48,746 --> 00:28:49,746
(sings)

989
00:28:49,746 --> 00:28:50,746
♫ Oh Sally Frank, oh Sally Frank,

990
00:28:50,746 --> 00:28:52,706
♫ Eats a lot of poisoned corn ♫

991
00:28:52,706 --> 00:28:53,866
(chuckles)

992
00:28:53,866 --> 00:28:55,248
- Just wrapped a gum
wrapper around a fuse.

993
00:28:55,248 --> 00:28:56,928
- Colonel, try it again.

994
00:28:56,928 --> 00:28:59,168
I'm sure it will work now.

995
00:28:59,168 --> 00:29:00,168
Are you there?

996
00:29:00,168 --> 00:29:01,288
Colonel!

997
00:29:01,288 --> 00:29:02,121
- Now hang up on your end.

998
00:29:02,121 --> 00:29:02,954
Hang up!

999
00:29:02,954 --> 00:29:03,787
I'm hanging up.

1000
00:29:03,787 --> 00:29:06,537
(intrepid music)

1001
00:29:08,373 --> 00:29:09,206
- I love this song.

1002
00:29:09,206 --> 00:29:11,848
- What a way to die, listening
to the Tijuana Brass.

1003
00:29:11,848 --> 00:29:13,688
(chuckles)

1004
00:29:13,688 --> 00:29:14,688
(sings)

1005
00:29:14,688 --> 00:29:17,128
♫ This is the song about
the Bacchus Three crew,

1006
00:29:17,128 --> 00:29:21,290
♫ They're gonna die from all the heat,

1007
00:29:21,290 --> 00:29:25,050
♫ he tried to kill them with a forklift,

1008
00:29:25,050 --> 00:29:26,050
♫ Away! ♫

1009
00:29:26,050 --> 00:29:28,133
(groans)

1010
00:29:28,970 --> 00:29:30,330
- That looks like a real
uncomfortable Halloween costume.

1011
00:29:30,330 --> 00:29:32,330
(pants)

1012
00:29:33,770 --> 00:29:35,603
- I got to keep going!

1013
00:29:36,610 --> 00:29:39,943
- Got to get it with girl in hot pants--

1014
00:29:42,570 --> 00:29:44,653
(groans)

1015
00:29:46,850 --> 00:29:49,130
- I know what it is, they're
flying through Developer Four.

1016
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:50,963
(zap)

1017
00:29:51,970 --> 00:29:55,332
- Oh man, no more Jello shots, I mean it.

1018
00:29:55,332 --> 00:29:56,452
This is it.

1019
00:29:56,452 --> 00:29:57,952
Now, I quit today.

1020
00:29:59,012 --> 00:30:00,012
(zapping)

1021
00:30:00,012 --> 00:30:02,132
- There's a drum major
flying the ship now.

1022
00:30:02,132 --> 00:30:03,172
- Captain!

1023
00:30:03,172 --> 00:30:04,612
We've got the engines working.

1024
00:30:04,612 --> 00:30:06,812
Now if we can just get
away from that star!

1025
00:30:06,812 --> 00:30:08,252
- Let me have my coffee first, okay?

1026
00:30:08,252 --> 00:30:10,372
I'm not good without it.

1027
00:30:10,372 --> 00:30:11,972
(sings along with background music)

1028
00:30:11,972 --> 00:30:15,012
♫ This is the song, about
the crew's condition ♫

1029
00:30:15,012 --> 00:30:16,292
- Just a few seconds, and we'll be safe.

1030
00:30:16,292 --> 00:30:19,092
♫ They'll all be alive,
they're gonna puke,

1031
00:30:19,092 --> 00:30:23,259
♫ He tried to kill me with a forklift ♫

1032
00:30:29,177 --> 00:30:30,116
- What's going on?

1033
00:30:30,116 --> 00:30:31,556
(vocalizing)

1034
00:30:31,556 --> 00:30:33,476
- This is going to be great,
speakers on the porch,

1035
00:30:33,476 --> 00:30:34,916
oh well.

1036
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:36,316
- That ought to keep the
cooling system going.

1037
00:30:36,316 --> 00:30:37,558
Just one more connection.

1038
00:30:37,558 --> 00:30:39,958
(beeps)

1039
00:30:39,958 --> 00:30:41,278
Okay, good!

1040
00:30:41,278 --> 00:30:42,638
- Looks good, tastes good, is good!

1041
00:30:42,638 --> 00:30:43,998
- Good for me.

1042
00:30:43,998 --> 00:30:45,258
- Colonel, I got the cooling system fixed.

1043
00:30:45,258 --> 00:30:46,378
Can you get her on course?

1044
00:30:46,378 --> 00:30:48,938
- It's no use, we're too late now.

1045
00:30:48,938 --> 00:30:49,978
- It's very hot.

1046
00:30:49,978 --> 00:30:50,978
- We've gotta go on!

1047
00:30:50,978 --> 00:30:52,018
Try again!

1048
00:30:52,018 --> 00:30:53,298
- I can't make it.

1049
00:30:53,298 --> 00:30:54,378
- It didn't--

1050
00:30:54,378 --> 00:30:55,378
- What?

1051
00:30:55,378 --> 00:30:56,378
- Colonel!

1052
00:30:56,378 --> 00:30:57,378
Can you hear me?

1053
00:30:57,378 --> 00:30:58,211
Colonel?

1054
00:30:58,211 --> 00:30:59,044
(gasps)

1055
00:30:59,044 --> 00:30:59,877
- It's very hot!

1056
00:30:59,877 --> 00:31:00,710
Hot in here.

1057
00:31:00,710 --> 00:31:01,543
Hey.

1058
00:31:01,543 --> 00:31:03,152
(muttering)

1059
00:31:03,152 --> 00:31:05,652
(grunts)

1060
00:31:05,652 --> 00:31:08,774
- Oh no, we're getting
closer to that star!

1061
00:31:08,774 --> 00:31:10,134
Looks like I'd better take over!

1062
00:31:10,134 --> 00:31:11,134
(grunts)

1063
00:31:11,134 --> 00:31:12,894
- Fine, but towel off first or something.

1064
00:31:12,894 --> 00:31:13,894
(grunts)

1065
00:31:13,894 --> 00:31:15,614
Not a kid anymore.

1066
00:31:15,614 --> 00:31:17,294
- They're having the film
steam cleaned right now.

1067
00:31:17,294 --> 00:31:19,214
- Well, they need it.

1068
00:31:19,214 --> 00:31:20,214
(grunts)

1069
00:31:20,214 --> 00:31:21,214
- Captain!

1070
00:31:21,214 --> 00:31:23,534
I got it fixed, it's all working again!

1071
00:31:23,534 --> 00:31:25,094
- Great, just in time to see us die.

1072
00:31:25,094 --> 00:31:28,094
- I got it working, get going!

1073
00:31:28,094 --> 00:31:30,694
- Oh wait, who's turn is it to pass out?

1074
00:31:30,694 --> 00:31:33,614
- I think the audience is
ready to pass out about now.

1075
00:31:33,614 --> 00:31:35,614
(yells)

1076
00:31:37,254 --> 00:31:38,574
(clicking)

1077
00:31:38,574 --> 00:31:41,178
- What is he, starting
the Wild Mouse Ride?

1078
00:31:41,178 --> 00:31:43,178
(blasting)

1079
00:31:43,178 --> 00:31:44,618
- Ignition!

1080
00:31:44,618 --> 00:31:45,618
- Yes.

1081
00:31:45,618 --> 00:31:46,698
- We're gonna make it!

1082
00:31:46,698 --> 00:31:47,818
- Colonel?

1083
00:31:47,818 --> 00:31:50,058
Faster, full thrust.

1084
00:31:50,058 --> 00:31:52,058
- You want to go faster?

1085
00:31:52,058 --> 00:31:53,258
(clicking)

1086
00:31:53,258 --> 00:31:54,091
- Full thrust?

1087
00:31:54,091 --> 00:31:54,924
No, no.

1088
00:31:54,924 --> 00:31:55,757
Not you, the engines!

1089
00:31:55,757 --> 00:31:56,590
(chuckles)

1090
00:31:56,590 --> 00:31:57,423
(blasting)

1091
00:31:57,423 --> 00:31:58,256
- Kid power!

1092
00:31:58,256 --> 00:32:00,162
Red, yellow, black, white!

1093
00:32:00,162 --> 00:32:01,063
- We did it!

1094
00:32:01,063 --> 00:32:01,896
We're going!

1095
00:32:01,896 --> 00:32:02,729
- We did it!

1096
00:32:02,729 --> 00:32:04,166
We killed 20 minutes of movie!

1097
00:32:04,166 --> 00:32:04,999
(cheers)

1098
00:32:04,999 --> 00:32:07,506
- I'll take the controls.

1099
00:32:07,506 --> 00:32:12,288
- I guess you don't need
ol' Captain Joe anymore.

1100
00:32:12,288 --> 00:32:14,108
- Graduates, 'til you begin the journey

1101
00:32:14,108 --> 00:32:16,668
of the rest of your life, we
may never pass this way again,

1102
00:32:16,668 --> 00:32:17,668
and--

1103
00:32:17,668 --> 00:32:19,068
(groans)

1104
00:32:19,068 --> 00:32:20,308
- I'm missing graduation.

1105
00:32:20,308 --> 00:32:22,391
The music started, oh no!

1106
00:32:24,053 --> 00:32:26,228
(sniffs)

1107
00:32:26,228 --> 00:32:28,588
- Oh, it looks like the
ten-perature is coming down.

1108
00:32:28,588 --> 00:32:30,228
(snickers)

1109
00:32:30,228 --> 00:32:31,428
- See?

1110
00:32:31,428 --> 00:32:32,428
I'm not even stinky.

1111
00:32:32,428 --> 00:32:33,588
(chuckles)

1112
00:32:33,588 --> 00:32:34,588
- Thank you.

1113
00:32:35,468 --> 00:32:36,470
- Ken?

1114
00:32:36,470 --> 00:32:37,470
- Get outta my seat!

1115
00:32:37,470 --> 00:32:41,070
- You know, you both did a terrific job.

1116
00:32:41,070 --> 00:32:43,230
I won't forget it.

1117
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:46,270
- This old creep pulled
us through one more time.

1118
00:32:46,270 --> 00:32:48,520
- You're cute, both of you.

1119
00:32:50,412 --> 00:32:52,272
- Thanks again, Bacchus Three.

1120
00:32:52,272 --> 00:32:53,272
Bacchus!

1121
00:32:53,272 --> 00:32:54,312
- Good job.

1122
00:32:54,312 --> 00:32:55,145
- Now you've done it again.

1123
00:32:55,145 --> 00:32:57,232
(laughs)

1124
00:32:57,232 --> 00:32:58,065
(altogether)

1125
00:32:58,065 --> 00:32:59,302
- Mighty Jack.

1126
00:32:59,302 --> 00:33:00,502
Yeah.

1127
00:33:00,502 --> 00:33:01,669
- Mighty Jack?

1128
00:33:03,504 --> 00:33:04,624
- I'm quite a guy, really.

1129
00:33:04,624 --> 00:33:05,457
You know?

1130
00:33:09,624 --> 00:33:10,664
- So?

1131
00:33:10,664 --> 00:33:11,664
- Hey Dan?

1132
00:33:11,664 --> 00:33:13,264
Come on, we're goin' fishin'!

1133
00:33:13,264 --> 00:33:14,464
You promised.

1134
00:33:14,464 --> 00:33:15,464
- How you doing?

1135
00:33:15,464 --> 00:33:16,464
- Still a little groggy.

1136
00:33:16,464 --> 00:33:17,744
- Is everybody alright?

1137
00:33:17,744 --> 00:33:18,577
- Not too bad.

1138
00:33:18,577 --> 00:33:19,410
- I feel great.

1139
00:33:19,410 --> 00:33:20,454
Ready for a workout.

1140
00:33:20,454 --> 00:33:21,616
- Yeah, you got spunk.

1141
00:33:21,616 --> 00:33:22,896
I hate spunk.

1142
00:33:22,896 --> 00:33:23,979
- What is it?

1143
00:33:24,856 --> 00:33:26,218
- [Man On Phone] This is
your morning call, sir.

1144
00:33:26,218 --> 00:33:27,898
We'll be expecting you all downstairs

1145
00:33:27,898 --> 00:33:29,258
in an hour for some tennis.

1146
00:33:29,258 --> 00:33:30,578
- Is this the morning ZOO guys?

1147
00:33:30,578 --> 00:33:31,738
(laughs)

1148
00:33:31,738 --> 00:33:33,178
- Yeah, I'll go string my racket.

1149
00:33:33,178 --> 00:33:34,778
Say, what happened to room service?

1150
00:33:34,778 --> 00:33:35,778
- [Man On Phone] Sorry, sir.

1151
00:33:35,778 --> 00:33:38,140
I'm afraid our guests have
to cook their own breakfasts.

1152
00:33:38,140 --> 00:33:39,900
- Enough of the good-natured ribbing, bye!

1153
00:33:39,900 --> 00:33:40,733
- You bet.

1154
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,040
- I love it.

1155
00:33:43,040 --> 00:33:46,123
(upbeat techy music)

1156
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:51,560
- Please hold your present
position for the moment,

1157
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:53,562
we will be giving you your
landing instructions shortly.

1158
00:33:53,562 --> 00:33:54,762
- Shortly?

1159
00:33:54,762 --> 00:33:56,179
What's the delay?

1160
00:33:57,682 --> 00:33:59,602
- They might have to clear
a landing space for us,

1161
00:33:59,602 --> 00:34:01,322
that's all.

1162
00:34:01,322 --> 00:34:03,882
Message received, we're
holding our position,

1163
00:34:03,882 --> 00:34:04,715
waiting to hear from you.

1164
00:34:04,715 --> 00:34:06,554
- All our best to Joan and the kids.

1165
00:34:06,554 --> 00:34:09,304
(blasting stops)

1166
00:34:10,674 --> 00:34:13,794
- So, looks like I'll park there, then.

1167
00:34:13,794 --> 00:34:14,994
Park on the street.

1168
00:34:14,994 --> 00:34:17,674
- I think I could speed things
up if I had a word with them.

1169
00:34:17,674 --> 00:34:18,834
- Oh, Mr. Connections.

1170
00:34:18,834 --> 00:34:20,167
Oh, Mr. Sarcasm.

1171
00:34:21,496 --> 00:34:24,296
- Colonel Yurulin calling
Saysar headquarters.

1172
00:34:24,296 --> 00:34:25,616
- [Man On Phone] Yurulin?

1173
00:34:25,616 --> 00:34:26,696
- Yep, we're number one!

1174
00:34:26,696 --> 00:34:28,376
- Your space command was
nice enough to rescue me

1175
00:34:28,376 --> 00:34:29,856
from a Carraru Prison.

1176
00:34:29,856 --> 00:34:32,056
I can vouch for every one of the crew.

1177
00:34:32,056 --> 00:34:34,296
We'd like to land on Saysar right away.

1178
00:34:34,296 --> 00:34:35,538
- Bite me?

1179
00:34:35,538 --> 00:34:37,738
Is that official?

1180
00:34:37,738 --> 00:34:40,155
(dark music)

1181
00:34:41,018 --> 00:34:42,458
- Say, what's the matter down there?

1182
00:34:42,458 --> 00:34:44,098
I'm used to having my official request

1183
00:34:44,098 --> 00:34:45,618
