to lead us to it.

1219
00:35:42,336 --> 00:35:44,656
They don't even know you down there.

1220
00:35:44,656 --> 00:35:46,296
- It's ridiculous.

1221
00:35:46,296 --> 00:35:47,776
Bunch of idiots!

1222
00:35:47,776 --> 00:35:49,296
- Ship of fools!

1223
00:35:49,296 --> 00:35:50,296
(dramatic music)

1224
00:35:50,296 --> 00:35:52,016
- What the heck is going on?

1225
00:35:52,016 --> 00:35:53,016
(engines sounding)

1226
00:35:53,016 --> 00:35:54,096
- Oh no, no.

1227
00:35:54,096 --> 00:35:55,656
(dramatic music)

1228
00:35:55,656 --> 00:35:57,096
It's starting over.

1229
00:35:57,096 --> 00:35:58,096
(yells)

1230
00:35:58,096 --> 00:35:59,216
- Oh boy.

1231
00:35:59,216 --> 00:36:01,256
- I'm gonna bust it again, when it's over.

1232
00:36:01,256 --> 00:36:03,978
- Is she really going out with him?

1233
00:36:03,978 --> 00:36:05,018
- That was just a warning.

1234
00:36:05,018 --> 00:36:06,298
Ken, keep your cool.

1235
00:36:06,298 --> 00:36:07,898
- You're wrong.

1236
00:36:07,898 --> 00:36:09,498
Those guys aren't kidding.

1237
00:36:09,498 --> 00:36:10,898
- I can't believe it.

1238
00:36:10,898 --> 00:36:12,978
- My own people would
never dare shoot at me!

1239
00:36:12,978 --> 00:36:15,178
- [Captain] Looks like they have.

1240
00:36:15,178 --> 00:36:16,178
Engines, full blast.

1241
00:36:16,178 --> 00:36:17,778
(blasting)

1242
00:36:17,778 --> 00:36:20,138
- I love the whole incoherent
Mighty Jack quality

1243
00:36:20,138 --> 00:36:21,221
of this film.

1244
00:36:25,348 --> 00:36:27,139
(shudders)

1245
00:36:27,139 --> 00:36:28,339
- Will you repeat that, please?

1246
00:36:28,339 --> 00:36:29,983
- It's kind of a (mumbles).

1247
00:36:29,983 --> 00:36:30,983
- I wet 'em.

1248
00:36:33,219 --> 00:36:36,219
- This week, join Jonny,
Hadji, Race Bannon and Bandit.

1249
00:36:36,219 --> 00:36:37,779
(barks)

1250
00:36:37,779 --> 00:36:38,779
Jonny Quest.

1251
00:36:39,859 --> 00:36:41,259
- We're surrounded.

1252
00:36:41,259 --> 00:36:43,926
They'll attack again any minute.

1253
00:36:46,179 --> 00:36:48,741
- Don't let insects
spoil your garden party.

1254
00:36:48,741 --> 00:36:50,139
- Captain!

1255
00:36:50,139 --> 00:36:51,339
- Pia Zadora?

1256
00:36:51,339 --> 00:36:52,172
No!

1257
00:36:53,499 --> 00:36:54,941
- Oh, no.

1258
00:36:54,941 --> 00:36:56,619
They're being attacked by Norelco razors!

1259
00:36:56,619 --> 00:36:58,181
- Even the name says, "Merry Christmas!"

1260
00:36:58,181 --> 00:37:01,014
(lasers shooting)

1261
00:37:02,701 --> 00:37:03,701
- Oh!

1262
00:37:03,701 --> 00:37:05,021
I'm gonna get them!

1263
00:37:05,021 --> 00:37:06,341
- It's too dark to go out on your bike.

1264
00:37:06,341 --> 00:37:08,301
Come back here.

1265
00:37:08,301 --> 00:37:10,221
- Don't fire back, try to make contact.

1266
00:37:10,221 --> 00:37:11,621
Tell them it's a mistake!

1267
00:37:11,621 --> 00:37:13,143
- What are you, Captain
Kirk all of a sudden?

1268
00:37:13,143 --> 00:37:15,463
- Say, this is for real.

1269
00:37:15,463 --> 00:37:17,283
Get ready to counter-attack!

1270
00:37:17,283 --> 00:37:18,763
- Yes, sir!

1271
00:37:18,763 --> 00:37:21,680
- Magic booze bottle, take me away!

1272
00:37:26,883 --> 00:37:28,423
- Ole!

1273
00:37:28,423 --> 00:37:30,923
(laser fires)

1274
00:37:34,425 --> 00:37:35,945
- Breaked at it!

1275
00:37:35,945 --> 00:37:37,645
- Oh, is killing fun, Ken?

1276
00:37:37,645 --> 00:37:39,445
Does it amuse you?

1277
00:37:39,445 --> 00:37:40,445
(sings along with music)

1278
00:37:40,445 --> 00:37:41,445
♫ Let's all watch Ken,

1279
00:37:41,445 --> 00:37:42,445
♫ As he kills the bad guys,

1280
00:37:42,445 --> 00:37:43,645
♫ They'll taste their steel,

1281
00:37:43,645 --> 00:37:46,285
♫ Then drink their own blood,

1282
00:37:46,285 --> 00:37:50,205
♫ They'll try to kill
him with a forklift ♫

1283
00:37:50,205 --> 00:37:51,685
I'm making this up as I go along.

1284
00:37:51,685 --> 00:37:54,268
- Faster, PussyKen, kill, kill!

1285
00:37:58,917 --> 00:38:00,005
- Alright, go.

1286
00:38:00,005 --> 00:38:01,325
- Like you've never go-ed before.

1287
00:38:01,325 --> 00:38:02,805
- I'll show 'em.

1288
00:38:02,805 --> 00:38:04,967
- I'll run away, then they'll
be sorry they picked on me.

1289
00:38:04,967 --> 00:38:06,884
(sobs)

1290
00:38:08,167 --> 00:38:10,607
(lasers shooting)

1291
00:38:10,607 --> 00:38:12,647
- Why is Ken behaving like this?

1292
00:38:12,647 --> 00:38:16,064
- Because it's bitter and it's his heart.

1293
00:38:19,127 --> 00:38:20,247
- Bang, bang.

1294
00:38:20,247 --> 00:38:21,497
Killing is fun.

1295
00:38:25,407 --> 00:38:26,447
(booms)

1296
00:38:26,447 --> 00:38:28,367
- Oh, and he picks up a spare!

1297
00:38:28,367 --> 00:38:30,367
- Yeah, so let's review the plot so far.

1298
00:38:30,367 --> 00:38:33,207
They went into outer space and, let's see.

1299
00:38:33,207 --> 00:38:34,727
(stammers)

1300
00:38:34,727 --> 00:38:39,171
They went into space, and
it's on the tip of my tongue.

1301
00:38:39,171 --> 00:38:40,891
- Oh, I know, I know.

1302
00:38:40,891 --> 00:38:42,611
They suffocated for awhile, and--

1303
00:38:42,611 --> 00:38:45,611
- And then came lots of explosions, and--

1304
00:38:45,611 --> 00:38:46,611
- Yeah, and

1305
00:38:46,611 --> 00:38:48,171
(explosion sounds)

1306
00:38:48,171 --> 00:38:49,838
- I think that's it.

1307
00:38:53,851 --> 00:38:55,011
- I really enjoyed that.

1308
00:38:55,011 --> 00:38:57,211
- You're sick, buddy.

1309
00:38:57,211 --> 00:38:58,371
- Now that they know where we are,

1310
00:38:58,371 --> 00:38:59,611
they're gonna send out the next wave.

1311
00:38:59,611 --> 00:39:01,011
- You know the old
saying, "eye for an eye."

1312
00:39:01,011 --> 00:39:02,011
(chuckles)

1313
00:39:02,011 --> 00:39:03,011
- Breakfasts and dentists.

1314
00:39:03,011 --> 00:39:04,211
(laughs)

1315
00:39:04,211 --> 00:39:05,491
- Here they come again!

1316
00:39:05,491 --> 00:39:07,091
- Ooh, catch 'em if you can!

1317
00:39:07,091 --> 00:39:09,131
- There's no way out of this, sir.

1318
00:39:09,131 --> 00:39:11,091
Sooner or later one of
them is gonna score a hit.

1319
00:39:11,091 --> 00:39:12,171
- Off the bong.

1320
00:39:12,171 --> 00:39:13,173
Woo!

1321
00:39:13,173 --> 00:39:14,413
- Can you guide us to a safe place

1322
00:39:14,413 --> 00:39:15,613
to make an emergency landing?

1323
00:39:15,613 --> 00:39:19,053
- Uh, my uncle's got a
planet, let's crash there.

1324
00:39:19,053 --> 00:39:20,333
- If you wanna stay alive,

1325
00:39:20,333 --> 00:39:21,613
you're gonna have to help us.

1326
00:39:21,613 --> 00:39:23,093
Where can we land?

1327
00:39:23,093 --> 00:39:24,693
- Well, I do know of a place.

1328
00:39:24,693 --> 00:39:25,526
- Alright.

1329
00:39:26,653 --> 00:39:28,013
Tell us where it is.

1330
00:39:28,013 --> 00:39:29,933
- Everyone calls it the Devil's Desert.

1331
00:39:29,933 --> 00:39:31,133
- Sounds pretty neat.

1332
00:39:31,133 --> 00:39:32,653
- If you're really
willing to take the risk,

1333
00:39:32,653 --> 00:39:34,413
I'll be glad to guide you.

1334
00:39:34,413 --> 00:39:36,253
- Okay, let's go.

1335
00:39:36,253 --> 00:39:37,773
- We're going to Vegas, everybody!

1336
00:39:37,773 --> 00:39:38,606
Woo!

1337
00:39:42,860 --> 00:39:44,895
- Looks like the big blue marble.

1338
00:39:44,895 --> 00:39:45,895
- Sure does.

1339
00:39:50,035 --> 00:39:52,315
- Okay let's see here,
there's Satan's triangle,

1340
00:39:52,315 --> 00:39:55,982
Lucifer's elbow, oh,
there's Devil's Desert.

1341
00:39:59,955 --> 00:40:02,795
- Flying over a teenage
skin eruption, sir.

1342
00:40:02,795 --> 00:40:03,628
- Eew.

1343
00:40:04,515 --> 00:40:06,475
(laughs)

1344
00:40:06,475 --> 00:40:07,475
- Huh?

1345
00:40:07,475 --> 00:40:08,595
- We're landing there?

1346
00:40:08,595 --> 00:40:11,437
- You gotta problem with that?

1347
00:40:11,437 --> 00:40:14,157
(humming)

1348
00:40:14,157 --> 00:40:15,157
- Nice effect, Bill.

1349
00:40:15,157 --> 00:40:16,637
- Hold on tight.

1350
00:40:16,637 --> 00:40:17,917
This is gonna be a rough one.

1351
00:40:17,917 --> 00:40:20,500
- We better learn to get along.

1352
00:40:26,745 --> 00:40:28,397
- Careful! Careful!

1353
00:40:28,397 --> 00:40:29,797
These sands are treacherous!

1354
00:40:29,797 --> 00:40:31,557
- They're headed straight for the dock!

1355
00:40:31,557 --> 00:40:32,717
(grunts)

1356
00:40:32,717 --> 00:40:34,967
(rumbling)

1357
00:40:41,119 --> 00:40:42,879
- You know this film
looks like it's scraping

1358
00:40:42,879 --> 00:40:43,919
the bottom.

1359
00:40:43,919 --> 00:40:46,759
- Well, should I let her down?

1360
00:40:46,759 --> 00:40:48,039
- Ah, note to myself.

1361
00:40:48,039 --> 00:40:50,539
Put landing gear on this baby.

1362
00:40:55,561 --> 00:40:56,394
(whispers)

1363
00:40:56,394 --> 00:40:58,125
- Arrakis, Dune.

1364
00:40:58,125 --> 00:40:59,375
Desert planets.

1365
00:41:02,605 --> 00:41:05,188
- Damn, just washed this thing.

1366
00:41:06,605 --> 00:41:08,725
- Looks like one of my
ski club overnights.

1367
00:41:08,725 --> 00:41:09,558
- Ooh!

1368
00:41:11,922 --> 00:41:14,961
- A planet that evolved from carob?

1369
00:41:14,961 --> 00:41:16,841
I don't think so.

1370
00:41:16,841 --> 00:41:19,091
- In-a-gadda-da-vida, baby!

1371
00:41:21,361 --> 00:41:23,444
(groans)

1372
00:41:25,523 --> 00:41:26,603
- Tammy!

1373
00:41:26,603 --> 00:41:27,603
Tammy!

1374
00:41:27,603 --> 00:41:29,283
- Tell me true!

1375
00:41:29,283 --> 00:41:30,686
- A girl, a grim old warrior
is supposed to be brave!

1376
00:41:30,686 --> 00:41:31,519
- Ken?

1377
00:41:31,519 --> 00:41:32,445
- Are you alright?

1378
00:41:32,445 --> 00:41:33,975
- Yes.

1379
00:41:33,975 --> 00:41:34,808
- Get up.

1380
00:41:38,087 --> 00:41:39,687
Sir!

1381
00:41:39,687 --> 00:41:41,354
- Foo-ball practice!

1382
00:41:44,528 --> 00:41:45,361
- What, what?

1383
00:41:45,361 --> 00:41:46,693
Who turned off the TV set?

1384
00:41:46,693 --> 00:41:48,013
- Bloody Marys all around!

1385
00:41:48,013 --> 00:41:49,013
(grunts)

1386
00:41:49,013 --> 00:41:50,333
- Come on, pull yourself together.

1387
00:41:50,333 --> 00:41:52,213
- You're telling him to
pull yourself together?

1388
00:41:52,213 --> 00:41:54,253
Ken, better check the others.

1389
00:41:54,253 --> 00:41:55,253
- Okay.

1390
00:41:55,253 --> 00:41:58,173
- Oh yeah, aye-aye, Captain.

1391
00:41:58,173 --> 00:41:59,173
- Dan?

1392
00:41:59,173 --> 00:42:00,423
Snap out of it!

1393
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:02,473
Billy!

1394
00:42:02,473 --> 00:42:03,373
- Don't be a hero!

1395
00:42:03,373 --> 00:42:04,893
- Colonel Yurulin!

1396
00:42:04,893 --> 00:42:05,726
(groans)

1397
00:42:05,726 --> 00:42:06,853
- Drive through clowns!

1398
00:42:06,853 --> 00:42:08,013
I want a sunrise biscuit!

1399
00:42:08,013 --> 00:42:09,373
Come on in there!

1400
00:42:09,373 --> 00:42:10,733
- Would you look at that?

1401
00:42:10,733 --> 00:42:12,493
So hot in here it feels like a steam bath.

1402
00:42:12,493 --> 00:42:14,055
- And me without a towel.

1403
00:42:14,055 --> 00:42:15,859
- Rocky, better get
the area on the screen.

1404
00:42:15,859 --> 00:42:16,692
- Okay.

1405
00:42:18,259 --> 00:42:19,739
- Oh wow, they gotta
watch their own reruns?

1406
00:42:19,739 --> 00:42:21,299
What a nightmare!

1407
00:42:21,299 --> 00:42:23,099
- I wonder how much damage we've done.

1408
00:42:23,099 --> 00:42:24,179
- I don't know.

1409
00:42:24,179 --> 00:42:26,099
I want every inch of
this craft checked out.

1410
00:42:26,099 --> 00:42:27,099
- Yes sir!

1411
00:42:27,099 --> 00:42:27,932
- Every inch.

1412
00:42:27,932 --> 00:42:28,765
- Even the inch under your seat?

1413
00:42:28,765 --> 00:42:30,219
- Every inch, get to it.

1414
00:42:30,219 --> 00:42:31,099
- Even the dirtiest inch in the kitchen?

1415
00:42:31,099 --> 00:42:31,932
- Every single inch.

1416
00:42:31,932 --> 00:42:33,339
- Even that inch--

1417
00:42:33,339 --> 00:42:35,881
- At least we're on the ground again.

1418
00:42:35,881 --> 00:42:37,733
Alright, I'd better go help the others.

1419
00:42:37,733 --> 00:42:40,816
(upbeat techy music)

1420
00:42:43,933 --> 00:42:45,293
- [Tom Servo] New, from
the Star Force line

1421
00:42:45,293 --> 00:42:46,533
of action figures, it's Captain Joe!

1422
00:42:46,533 --> 00:42:49,855
The boozy, brawling, bloated,
Bacchus Three commander

1423
00:42:49,855 --> 00:42:51,853
from the beloved Fugitive Aliens series!

1424
00:42:51,853 --> 00:42:53,293
- Dizzy Gillespie cheeks sold separately!

1425
00:42:53,293 --> 00:42:56,133
- Yes, he swaggers, he
staggers, and he even talks!

1426
00:42:56,133 --> 00:42:58,973
- Um, if I would do a
lot worse than throw with

1427
00:42:58,973 --> 00:43:01,533
a lot of Bacchus Three,
set 'em up, barkeep.

1428
00:43:01,533 --> 00:43:02,773
- Flask and travel bar not included.

1429
00:43:02,773 --> 00:43:03,773
(crash)

1430
00:43:03,773 --> 00:43:04,689
- Yes, with your Captain
Joe action figure,

1431
00:43:04,689 --> 00:43:06,009
you'll be in a constant
state of excitement

1432
00:43:06,009 --> 00:43:08,009
while he's in a state of denial.

1433
00:43:08,009 --> 00:43:09,929
- I only drink on the weekend.

1434
00:43:09,929 --> 00:43:11,012
I can drink--

1435
00:43:12,049 --> 00:43:13,449
- Existential void where prohibited.

1436
00:43:13,449 --> 00:43:15,249
- Sure, he's got a problem but you don't

1437
00:43:15,249 --> 00:43:16,149
have to watch him deteriorate,

1438
00:43:16,149 --> 00:43:18,589
after all, you've spent
nine ninety-five for him!

1439
00:43:18,589 --> 00:43:19,669
- Tax and license not included.

1440
00:43:19,669 --> 00:43:20,969
- You can have hours
of fun as you organize

1441
00:43:20,969 --> 00:43:23,209
a crisis intervention for Captain Joe!

1442
00:43:23,209 --> 00:43:26,729
- Captain Joe, I am not gonna sit here

1443
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:29,009
and watch you deteriorate.

1444
00:43:29,009 --> 00:43:30,011
(Joel speaking in woman's voice)

1445
00:43:30,011 --> 00:43:32,969
Captain Joe, Ken and
I had you over to eat.

1446
00:43:32,969 --> 00:43:36,731
You got drunk on cooking
sherry and made a pass at me

1447
00:43:36,731 --> 00:43:40,691
and threw up all over
the Malibu Dream House.

1448
00:43:40,691 --> 00:43:43,274
Captain Joe, dude, I loved you.

1449
00:43:44,171 --> 00:43:46,689
But I'm not gonna sit here and watch you

1450
00:43:46,689 --> 00:43:48,110
cowabungle your life.

1451
00:43:48,110 --> 00:43:48,943
(crash)

1452
00:43:48,943 --> 00:43:50,130
- And don't forget kids,

1453
00:43:50,130 --> 00:43:52,210
if Captain Joe refuses
to deal with the issues,

1454
00:43:52,210 --> 00:43:56,170
you can always try to
kill him with a forklift.

1455
00:43:56,170 --> 00:43:57,250
- 12 step workbook optional.

1456
00:43:57,250 --> 00:43:58,411
Product not included in some boxes.

1457
00:43:58,411 --> 00:44:00,411
Joe Namath netted slingshot
brief sold separately.

1458
00:44:00,411 --> 00:44:01,244
(buzzing)

1459
00:44:01,244 --> 00:44:03,331
(yells)

1460
00:44:03,331 --> 00:44:05,748
(doors open)

1461
00:44:13,551 --> 00:44:15,453
- Well, let's go.

1462
00:44:15,453 --> 00:44:16,453
- Hey, where are you going, Rocky?

1463
00:44:16,453 --> 00:44:17,333
- I'm sorry.

1464
00:44:17,333 --> 00:44:18,293
- Thanks.

1465
00:44:18,293 --> 00:44:19,126
- You and Tammy are staying here.

1466
00:44:19,126 --> 00:44:20,615
- What for?

1467
00:44:20,615 --> 00:44:22,895
- As soon as we've left,
I want you to bring back

1468
00:44:22,895 --> 00:44:25,135
us three to a safer place.

1469
00:44:25,135 --> 00:44:27,695
- Sir, do you think you're
doing the right thing?

1470
00:44:27,695 --> 00:44:28,855
- What do you mean?

1471
00:44:28,855 --> 00:44:31,775
- I was told, when the
mission is dangerous,

1472
00:44:31,775 --> 00:44:33,135
(clicking)

1473
00:44:33,135 --> 00:44:34,895
it's the older men who are
the ones to stay behind.

1474
00:44:34,895 --> 00:44:37,335
- Rocky, that's an order!

1475
00:44:37,335 --> 00:44:38,335
- Impressive eye contact.

1476
00:44:38,335 --> 00:44:40,015
- Sir, that's crazy.

1477
00:44:40,015 --> 00:44:41,495
You can't go on a forced
march through this desert

1478
00:44:41,495 --> 00:44:42,935
at your age, let me go!

1479
00:44:42,935 --> 00:44:45,135
- I'll command my own mission.

1480
00:44:45,135 --> 00:44:46,295
You--

1481
00:44:46,295 --> 00:44:47,295
- Pull my finger.

1482
00:44:47,295 --> 00:44:48,455
- Do as you're told.

1483
00:44:48,455 --> 00:44:49,535
I never shirk my responsibilities.

1484
00:44:49,535 --> 00:44:50,735
- Not even when my hip cracks.

1485
00:44:50,735 --> 00:44:53,485
(dramatic music)

1486
00:44:55,217 --> 00:44:56,217
- Rocky!

1487
00:44:56,217 --> 00:44:57,497
- Have you gone out of your mind?

1488
00:44:57,497 --> 00:44:59,817
- This is one order I can't obey.

1489
00:44:59,817 --> 00:45:01,377
- Disobey it over my dead body.

1490
00:45:01,377 --> 00:45:02,657
- Okay.

1491
00:45:02,657 --> 00:45:04,537
- [Tammy] Rocky, don't!

1492
00:45:04,537 --> 00:45:06,897
- Shoot me if you got the guts.

1493
00:45:06,897 --> 00:45:08,857
My orders still stand!

1494
00:45:08,857 --> 00:45:09,937
- Squeeze.

1495
00:45:09,937 --> 00:45:11,137
(gunshot)

1496
00:45:11,137 --> 00:45:12,617
(gasps)

1497
00:45:12,617 --> 00:45:13,617
(groans)

1498
00:45:13,617 --> 00:45:14,617
- Captain!

1499
00:45:14,617 --> 00:45:15,817
- Oh Captain, my Captain!

1500
00:45:15,817 --> 00:45:17,457
- Bitch, I'll kill ya for that!

1501
00:45:17,457 --> 00:45:18,697
- Don't get excited.

1502
00:45:18,697 --> 00:45:20,817
I wouldn't shoot my chief
with live ammunition.

1503
00:45:20,817 --> 00:45:21,977
It's a knockout dart.

1504
00:45:21,977 --> 00:45:23,457
- Of course it pierced his colon!

1505
00:45:23,457 --> 00:45:26,617
- It will just put him out of
commission for an hour or so.

1506
00:45:26,617 --> 00:45:28,217
Help me to get him someplace comfortable.

1507
00:45:28,217 --> 00:45:29,299
Ken, grab his legs.

1508
00:45:29,299 --> 00:45:31,979
Now men, we've got a
mission to accomplish.

1509
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:34,259
- This is gonna be the first
time he's passed out cold

1510
00:45:34,259 --> 00:45:35,899
and gonna wake up sober.

1511
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:36,899
(chuckles)

1512
00:45:36,899 --> 00:45:37,899
- Peek a boo!

1513
00:45:37,899 --> 00:45:39,859
- It's Abbott and Costello
in "Turning Japanese."

1514
00:45:39,859 --> 00:45:40,859
(vocalizing)

1515
00:45:40,859 --> 00:45:43,059
- All right, let's go.

1516
00:45:43,059 --> 00:45:45,819
(dramatic music)

1517
00:45:45,819 --> 00:45:47,539
- And man was born of woman,

1518
00:45:47,539 --> 00:45:50,579
and they both inhabited the earth.

1519
00:45:50,579 --> 00:45:53,859
- Tammy, I want you to contact us

1520
00:45:53,859 --> 00:45:56,659
as soon as you move Bacchus
Three to a safer place.

1521
00:45:56,659 --> 00:45:59,019
Call us on our micro radios.

1522
00:45:59,019 --> 00:46:00,019
- Right.

1523
00:46:00,019 --> 00:46:01,379
- We'll try to maintain
contact from our end.

1524
00:46:01,379 --> 00:46:02,459
And don't forget.

1525
00:46:02,459 --> 00:46:03,581
Keep us in radar range.

1526
00:46:03,581 --> 00:46:05,541
- You can count on it.

1527
00:46:05,541 --> 00:46:06,581
(coughs)

1528
00:46:06,581 --> 00:46:07,661
- Oh, and you better lock
up the liquor cabinet

1529
00:46:07,661 --> 00:46:09,101
and hide the key.

1530
00:46:09,101 --> 00:46:10,501
You know what I mean?

1531
00:46:10,501 --> 00:46:12,021
(singing along with music)

1532
00:46:12,021 --> 00:46:14,421
♫ We're headed for adventure,

1533
00:46:14,421 --> 00:46:18,088
♫ We'll leave Tammy behind,

1534
00:46:19,381 --> 00:46:22,903
♫ We're gonna pad up the film some more,

1535
00:46:22,903 --> 00:46:27,070
♫ And you'll fall asleep, three, four,

1536
00:46:28,663 --> 00:46:32,983
♫ We're climbing the sandy hill,

1537
00:46:32,983 --> 00:46:37,150
♫ Like you really care ♫

1538
00:46:39,520 --> 00:46:40,353
- Faster!

1539
00:46:40,353 --> 00:46:41,827
- Yes, sir!

1540
00:46:41,827 --> 00:46:42,827
- There's spiders all over me!

1541
00:46:42,827 --> 00:46:43,827
Get 'em off me!

1542
00:46:43,827 --> 00:46:44,827
Get 'em off me!

1543
00:46:44,827 --> 00:46:46,747
(sobs)

1544
00:46:46,747 --> 00:46:47,667
(groans)

1545
00:46:47,667 --> 00:46:48,947
- You know, it's the funniest sensation,

1546
00:46:48,947 --> 00:46:50,267
the room's not spinning.

1547
00:46:50,267 --> 00:46:51,100
Hmm.

1548
00:46:52,627 --> 00:46:53,747
- I'll kill that Rocky.

1549
00:46:53,747 --> 00:46:54,580
- Again?

1550
00:46:54,580 --> 00:46:56,859
(chuckles)

1551
00:46:56,859 --> 00:46:58,741
- I took the liberty of
changing your jumpsuit, sir.

1552
00:46:58,741 --> 00:46:59,574
- Captain!

1553
00:47:00,461 --> 00:47:01,381
- Are they in radar range?

1554
00:47:01,381 --> 00:47:02,681
- Yes sir.

1555
00:47:02,681 --> 00:47:04,081
They're right here on the screen.

1556
00:47:04,081 --> 00:47:06,241
22 degrees east north east.

1557
00:47:06,241 --> 00:47:08,408
(beeping)

1558
00:47:09,481 --> 00:47:10,921
- I'm not in right now, but if you'd like

1559
00:47:10,921 --> 00:47:12,641
to leave a message with my shoulder--

1560
00:47:12,641 --> 00:47:13,681
- Rocky.

1561
00:47:13,681 --> 00:47:14,681
- Again?

1562
00:47:14,681 --> 00:47:15,721
- Rocky!

1563
00:47:15,721 --> 00:47:17,681
- I read you loud and clear.

1564
00:47:17,681 --> 00:47:18,542
- Stop it.

1565
00:47:18,542 --> 00:47:19,662
- We're advancing on our objective.

1566
00:47:19,662 --> 00:47:21,302
- That was a dirty trick you played on me.

1567
00:47:21,302 --> 00:47:22,502
(clears throat)

1568
00:47:22,502 --> 00:47:23,862
- Why don't you court
marshal me over a cold beer

1569
00:47:23,862 --> 00:47:25,462
when this mission is over?

1570
00:47:25,462 --> 00:47:26,502
- And a shot?

1571
00:47:26,502 --> 00:47:27,502
- Alright.

1572
00:47:27,502 --> 00:47:29,223
I want you guys to be careful.

1573
00:47:29,223 --> 00:47:30,983
It's a very tricky operation.

1574
00:47:30,983 --> 00:47:32,103
- Yes sir.

1575
00:47:32,103 --> 00:47:34,383
And you get a good rest.

1576
00:47:34,383 --> 00:47:36,303
One of these days you'll
thank me for what I did.

1577
00:47:36,303 --> 00:47:38,303
- Shoulder phone off.

1578
00:47:38,303 --> 00:47:39,303
- Rocky.

1579
00:47:39,303 --> 00:47:40,303
- Again?

1580
00:47:40,303 --> 00:47:41,503
- Sorry.

1581
00:47:41,503 --> 00:47:43,623
(beeping)

1582
00:47:43,623 --> 00:47:45,063
- Pong?

1583
00:47:45,063 --> 00:47:45,896
Hmm.

1584
00:47:47,423 --> 00:47:48,463
- That Rocky.

1585
00:47:48,463 --> 00:47:49,503
- Again?

1586
00:47:49,503 --> 00:47:51,943
- I'll bust him when this is over.

1587
00:47:51,943 --> 00:47:53,623
(giggles)

1588
00:47:53,623 --> 00:47:57,170
- Sorry, I was thinking
of something else, sir.

1589
00:47:57,170 --> 00:47:58,003
(singing to music)

1590
00:47:58,003 --> 00:48:01,005
♫ We are marching on a big sand hill,

1591
00:48:01,005 --> 00:48:03,505
♫ We realize you've had your fill,

1592
00:48:03,505 --> 00:48:05,765
♫ As we march up on this big sand hill. ♫

1593
00:48:05,765 --> 00:48:06,765
- Just stop.

1594
00:48:06,765 --> 00:48:07,598
- Hey, corn.

1595
00:48:07,598 --> 00:48:08,431
Hey, corn!

1596
00:48:08,431 --> 00:48:09,348
- Get down!

1597
00:48:11,164 --> 00:48:12,807
- There's a watch tower.

1598
00:48:12,807 --> 00:48:15,427
- Oh, but I kid (mumbles)
ladies and gentlemen!

1599
00:48:15,427 --> 00:48:16,260
Love them.

1600
00:48:18,502 --> 00:48:21,829
- Hey, check it out,
they're fighting ZZ Top!

1601
00:48:21,829 --> 00:48:23,629
(dramatic music)

1602
00:48:23,629 --> 00:48:24,546
- Hey, hey.

1603
00:48:26,709 --> 00:48:27,709
Oh hi, Evan.

1604
00:48:31,269 --> 00:48:35,436
- I think they swiped this
music from Mission: Impossible.

1605
00:48:39,391 --> 00:48:40,711
- Get in as close as you can.

1606
00:48:40,711 --> 00:48:42,471
I'll try to divert the guards.

1607
00:48:42,471 --> 00:48:43,551
- And watch out for the percussionist.

1608
00:48:43,551 --> 00:48:46,151
They might have tambourines.

1609
00:48:46,151 --> 00:48:47,151
- Let go of my leg.

1610
00:48:47,151 --> 00:48:47,984
- What's the matter?

1611
00:48:47,984 --> 00:48:49,035
Don't you trust me?

1612
00:48:49,035 --> 00:48:51,155
- What guarantee do we have
that you won't double-cross us?

1613
00:48:51,155 --> 00:48:52,795
- Oh, I'll leave you my keys.

1614
00:48:52,795 --> 00:48:54,555
- Look, if you attack that post head-on,

1615
00:48:54,555 --> 00:48:56,395
those machine guns will
mow you down in a matter

1616
00:48:56,395 --> 00:48:57,475
of seconds.

1617
00:48:57,475 --> 00:48:58,475
- Hey, Moe!

1618
00:48:58,475 --> 00:49:00,642
- You know the way I feel.

1619
00:49:01,675 --> 00:49:03,837
I've got a score to
