1886
00:59:02,347 --> 00:59:04,427
- So you can thoroughly bore the viewers.

1887
00:59:04,427 --> 00:59:06,927
(grand music)

1888
00:59:09,027 --> 00:59:10,267
- You guys, I'm having a hard time feeling

1889
00:59:10,267 --> 00:59:11,787
how big this is, can we
have something on the screen

1890
00:59:11,787 --> 00:59:13,547
to figure out the scale, here?

1891
00:59:13,547 --> 00:59:15,469
It would be helpful.

1892
00:59:15,469 --> 00:59:17,029
- Attention, attention.

1893
00:59:17,029 --> 00:59:18,629
This is field marshal Tulsa,
your commander in chief.

1894
00:59:18,629 --> 00:59:20,469
- And grand poo-bah.

1895
00:59:20,469 --> 00:59:21,909
- I am proud to announce
that a new age has begun

1896
00:59:21,909 --> 00:59:23,309
for the people of Saysar--

1897
00:59:23,309 --> 00:59:24,309
- Oh, that explains the crystals.

1898
00:59:24,309 --> 00:59:25,309
(murmuring)

1899
00:59:25,309 --> 00:59:26,629
- From this moment on,
with our superior weapons

1900
00:59:26,629 --> 00:59:28,789
and military strength, we
can meet any challenge.

1901
00:59:28,789 --> 00:59:31,349
Not even the supposedly
invincible Wolf Raiders

1902
00:59:31,349 --> 00:59:34,869
from ValNastar can threaten us any more.

1903
00:59:34,869 --> 00:59:36,249
From now on we should
be able to crush their--

1904
00:59:36,249 --> 00:59:37,809
- Sorry, ladies.

1905
00:59:37,809 --> 00:59:39,331
- And destroy their very planet.

1906
00:59:39,331 --> 00:59:41,691
- Lunch today is chicken fried
steak and whipped potatoes.

1907
00:59:41,691 --> 00:59:43,971
- All ready to dominate the world!

1908
00:59:43,971 --> 00:59:45,831
Sir, we've achieved
the final breakthrough.

1909
00:59:45,831 --> 00:59:46,831
We're getting ready to--

1910
00:59:46,831 --> 00:59:48,031
- No speeches, soldier!

1911
00:59:48,031 --> 00:59:49,111
Get back to your post!

1912
00:59:49,111 --> 00:59:50,151
- Excuse me, sir.

1913
00:59:50,151 --> 00:59:51,911
I promise to pay more
attention to my duties.

1914
00:59:51,911 --> 00:59:52,911
- What a dope.

1915
00:59:52,911 --> 00:59:53,911
Hit 'em.

1916
00:59:53,911 --> 00:59:54,744
Come on.

1917
00:59:56,951 --> 00:59:57,955
- Halt!

1918
00:59:57,955 --> 00:59:59,071
Nobody's allowed past this point.

1919
00:59:59,071 --> 01:00:00,631
- You must be a new recruit.

1920
01:00:00,631 --> 01:00:01,791
- No sir, a blue recruit.

1921
01:00:01,791 --> 01:00:02,791
- Yes, sir.

1922
01:00:02,791 --> 01:00:03,911
Right away.

1923
01:00:03,911 --> 01:00:05,078
Out of my way.

1924
01:00:07,951 --> 01:00:09,991
- Sir, I was ordered not to
let anyone pass this point.

1925
01:00:09,991 --> 01:00:11,071
- These men are alright.

1926
01:00:11,071 --> 01:00:13,031
- They're really good guys,
especially that chopper.

1927
01:00:13,031 --> 01:00:14,433
He's a nut.

1928
01:00:14,433 --> 01:00:16,100
- All done in there?

1929
01:00:21,873 --> 01:00:23,513
- It's a Super Tom Servo!

1930
01:00:23,513 --> 01:00:25,233
With thrust busters and glass packs!

1931
01:00:25,233 --> 01:00:26,473
Wow!

1932
01:00:26,473 --> 01:00:27,553
- Tunnel ram.

1933
01:00:27,553 --> 01:00:28,553
Four barrel.

1934
01:00:28,553 --> 01:00:29,713
Chopped and channeled.

1935
01:00:29,713 --> 01:00:30,546
Cool.

1936
01:00:31,913 --> 01:00:33,113
- Look at that!

1937
01:00:33,113 --> 01:00:34,233
Like a beating heart!

1938
01:00:34,233 --> 01:00:35,513
- Like a beating heart Liberal.

1939
01:00:35,513 --> 01:00:37,433
(coughs)

1940
01:00:37,433 --> 01:00:38,713
- Dan, you plant the time bomb.

1941
01:00:38,713 --> 01:00:39,546
- Okay.

1942
01:00:45,641 --> 01:00:46,555
- Wait, they're going to destroy it

1943
01:00:46,555 --> 01:00:48,635
with refrigerator magnets?

1944
01:00:48,635 --> 01:00:51,595
- Yes, my detachment was on maneuvers,

1945
01:00:51,595 --> 01:00:54,159
in the northernmost part of the country--

1946
01:00:54,159 --> 01:00:56,275
- Yeah, it was a blast, we had fun.

1947
01:00:56,275 --> 01:00:58,775
- You're a sleek young fellow.

1948
01:00:59,630 --> 01:01:00,880
Thin, charming.

1949
01:01:01,955 --> 01:01:02,955
- Yes, sir.

1950
01:01:02,955 --> 01:01:03,955
I know that, sir.

1951
01:01:03,955 --> 01:01:05,115
We had a competition in our unit.

1952
01:01:05,115 --> 01:01:06,195
- I was the bluest.

1953
01:01:06,195 --> 01:01:07,715
- That's why I was selected for guard duty

1954
01:01:07,715 --> 01:01:09,035
at this installation.

1955
01:01:09,035 --> 01:01:10,675
- You've created quite a
little world for yourself,

1956
01:01:10,675 --> 01:01:11,508
I see.

1957
01:01:16,250 --> 01:01:17,437
- Hide the bomb.

1958
01:01:17,437 --> 01:01:18,677
It's in the room with that kid.

1959
01:01:18,677 --> 01:01:19,717
- Open the door!

1960
01:01:19,717 --> 01:01:20,797
I haven't got all day!

1961
01:01:20,797 --> 01:01:22,837
- Well I do, but I don't
want to give it up for this

1962
01:01:22,837 --> 01:01:24,757
is what I mean.

1963
01:01:24,757 --> 01:01:25,837
- Everything all right?

1964
01:01:25,837 --> 01:01:26,837
- Yes, sir.

1965
01:01:26,837 --> 01:01:27,837
Everything's just fine.

1966
01:01:27,837 --> 01:01:29,254
- Good, let's go.

1967
01:01:31,429 --> 01:01:33,837
- Bye, thanks for the check up.

1968
01:01:33,837 --> 01:01:34,670
So cool.

1969
01:01:43,399 --> 01:01:44,399
- Thanks.

1970
01:01:44,399 --> 01:01:45,959
- You're a fine soldier.

1971
01:01:45,959 --> 01:01:47,679
The next time I see your commander,

1972
01:01:47,679 --> 01:01:49,239
I'll tell him you're doing a good job.

1973
01:01:49,239 --> 01:01:50,359
- Oh, thank you, Colonel.

1974
01:01:50,359 --> 01:01:51,399
- Let's do lunch.

1975
01:01:51,399 --> 01:01:52,232
You're it.

1976
01:01:53,439 --> 01:01:57,531
- I could talk to that guy
until I'm blue in the face.

1977
01:01:57,531 --> 01:01:59,698
(humming)

1978
01:02:02,881 --> 01:02:04,361
- Thanks for keeping him distracted.

1979
01:02:04,361 --> 01:02:05,763
The time bomb is ready to go off.

1980
01:02:05,763 --> 01:02:07,963
- Oh, he's a swell kid,
hate to see him die.

1981
01:02:07,963 --> 01:02:11,046
(upbeat techy music)

1982
01:02:15,845 --> 01:02:18,012
- They're playing my song!

1983
01:02:19,925 --> 01:02:23,925
- Calculating number 15,
Eine Kleine Nachtmusik.

1984
01:02:26,040 --> 01:02:27,805
- Masterpiece Theatre is brought to you by

1985
01:02:27,805 --> 01:02:30,722
a grant from the Mobil Corporation.

1986
01:02:32,365 --> 01:02:33,645
- You can't just stand there, sir.

1987
01:02:33,645 --> 01:02:34,562
- Watch me.

1988
01:02:35,765 --> 01:02:38,007
- We've got to get out of here.

1989
01:02:38,007 --> 01:02:39,887
- This is our Saysar anthem.

1990
01:02:39,887 --> 01:02:40,720
- So what?

1991
01:02:41,607 --> 01:02:44,007
- Every day at this hour,
we all stand at attention

1992
01:02:44,007 --> 01:02:46,687
and renew our loyalty to the homeland.

1993
01:02:46,687 --> 01:02:47,687
- That's great.

1994
01:02:47,687 --> 01:02:49,247
While the others are
standing at attention,

1995
01:02:49,247 --> 01:02:50,607
we'll get out.

1996
01:02:50,607 --> 01:02:51,607
- Yeah, that's great.

1997
01:02:51,607 --> 01:02:52,647
You stand at attention
and I'll pick you up

1998
01:02:52,647 --> 01:02:53,647
and carry you, come on!

1999
01:02:53,647 --> 01:02:55,367
- Hey, are those Blaupunkt speakers?

2000
01:02:55,367 --> 01:02:56,567
They sound great.

2001
01:02:56,567 --> 01:02:59,729
- And the home of the brave!

2002
01:02:59,729 --> 01:03:01,369
(spits)

2003
01:03:01,369 --> 01:03:02,769
- Hey buddy!

2004
01:03:02,769 --> 01:03:03,769
- What's wrong?

2005
01:03:03,769 --> 01:03:05,609
- Can he hear?

2006
01:03:05,609 --> 01:03:06,609
- Colonel!

2007
01:03:06,609 --> 01:03:08,049
Psst, Colonel!

2008
01:03:08,049 --> 01:03:09,649
- Ex-nay on the edge-play!

2009
01:03:09,649 --> 01:03:11,171
- It's that music!

2010
01:03:11,171 --> 01:03:13,011
It has an effect on him.

2011
01:03:13,011 --> 01:03:14,731
When he hears it he snaps to attention.

2012
01:03:14,731 --> 01:03:16,971
- That guy's crazy!

2013
01:03:16,971 --> 01:03:19,171
We've got no time for patriotism now!

2014
01:03:19,171 --> 01:03:20,491
- That bomb is about to go off.

2015
01:03:20,491 --> 01:03:21,491
Colonel!

2016
01:03:21,491 --> 01:03:22,491
We gotta get out of here!

2017
01:03:22,491 --> 01:03:23,611
Come on down, sir,
there's no time to lose!

2018
01:03:23,611 --> 01:03:25,011
- Huh?

2019
01:03:25,011 --> 01:03:26,691
- My country needs me!

2020
01:03:26,691 --> 01:03:27,691
- Colonel!

2021
01:03:27,691 --> 01:03:28,771
- You know his country would win more wars

2022
01:03:28,771 --> 01:03:30,411
if it's national anthem was shorter.

2023
01:03:30,411 --> 01:03:31,651
- What happened to you?

2024
01:03:31,651 --> 01:03:33,984
- Somebody fingerpainted me!

2025
01:03:34,931 --> 01:03:35,931
(mutters)

2026
01:03:35,931 --> 01:03:37,171
- What?

2027
01:03:37,171 --> 01:03:39,131
- Get off my chest!

2028
01:03:39,131 --> 01:03:40,131
- Red alert!

2029
01:03:40,131 --> 01:03:41,131
Red alert!

2030
01:03:41,131 --> 01:03:42,131
Message received.

2031
01:03:42,131 --> 01:03:43,251
Nobody gets in here.

2032
01:03:43,251 --> 01:03:44,773
- Without a tuxedo and
a note from Mr. Gotti.

2033
01:03:44,773 --> 01:03:45,773
- You can't go in there!

2034
01:03:45,773 --> 01:03:47,733
- Outta my way!

2035
01:03:47,733 --> 01:03:48,733
- Infidel.

2036
01:03:48,733 --> 01:03:50,133
- Stay where you are!

2037
01:03:50,133 --> 01:03:51,453
One more step and I'll shoot!

2038
01:03:51,453 --> 01:03:52,733
(blast)

2039
01:03:52,733 --> 01:03:53,733
- He didn't take a step, what is he?

2040
01:03:53,733 --> 01:03:54,733
A Chicago cop?

2041
01:03:54,733 --> 01:03:55,773
That guy?

2042
01:03:55,773 --> 01:03:56,973
- Oh look, he's doing Joe Cocker.

2043
01:03:56,973 --> 01:03:58,453
(sings)

2044
01:03:58,453 --> 01:04:00,195
♫ What would you think? ♫

2045
01:04:00,195 --> 01:04:01,715
- Arby's just lost one good worker.

2046
01:04:01,715 --> 01:04:03,515
He was the best damn fry cook they had.

2047
01:04:03,515 --> 01:04:04,875
(clicks tongue)

2048
01:04:04,875 --> 01:04:06,435
Adios, sweet friend.

2049
01:04:06,435 --> 01:04:09,102
- Space Camp, with Kate Capshaw.

2050
01:04:11,955 --> 01:04:15,155
- We are unable to reach
the primary target, sir.

2051
01:04:15,155 --> 01:04:16,875
We will go to alternate target at Makiba.

2052
01:04:16,875 --> 01:04:19,239
- Captain, it's 15 minutes.

2053
01:04:19,239 --> 01:04:20,279
- We're not famous anymore.

2054
01:04:20,279 --> 01:04:21,719
- Ken and the others aren't out,

2055
01:04:21,719 --> 01:04:23,639
there's something wrong, sir.

2056
01:04:23,639 --> 01:04:25,159
- I have confidence in them.

2057
01:04:25,159 --> 01:04:26,679
They're all professionals.

2058
01:04:26,679 --> 01:04:29,604
- Yeah, I'll be inside
a bottle if you need me.

2059
01:04:29,604 --> 01:04:32,021
- I hate patronizing answers.

2060
01:04:36,106 --> 01:04:38,606
(sonic waves)

2061
01:04:39,703 --> 01:04:40,903
(screams)

2062
01:04:40,903 --> 01:04:42,563
- Prisoners are baked, not fried.

2063
01:04:42,563 --> 01:04:43,963
- Ken!

2064
01:04:43,963 --> 01:04:44,796
- Billy!

2065
01:04:46,803 --> 01:04:48,463
- Do not attempt to adjust your TV.

2066
01:04:48,463 --> 01:04:49,463
- Don't wait for me, go on ahead.

2067
01:04:49,463 --> 01:04:51,383
(blasts)

2068
01:04:51,383 --> 01:04:52,423
- Oh, wait!

2069
01:04:52,423 --> 01:04:54,103
Hit the wrong guy.

2070
01:04:54,103 --> 01:04:55,103
- Billy!

2071
01:04:55,103 --> 01:04:56,265
Save yourself!

2072
01:04:56,265 --> 01:04:57,265
- [Voiceover] There they are!

2073
01:04:57,265 --> 01:04:58,505
- Laser wall by Peter Max.

2074
01:04:58,505 --> 01:05:00,755
(shooting)

2075
01:05:02,345 --> 01:05:03,465
(humming along with music)

2076
01:05:03,465 --> 01:05:04,465
- Billy!

2077
01:05:04,465 --> 01:05:05,867
Don't try to fight them off, run for it!

2078
01:05:05,867 --> 01:05:06,987
- I'll come back for you, Dan!

2079
01:05:06,987 --> 01:05:07,820
- Yeah, right.

2080
01:05:07,820 --> 01:05:09,067
He'll never see him again.

2081
01:05:09,067 --> 01:05:09,987
(shooting)

2082
01:05:09,987 --> 01:05:11,667
- This is great.

2083
01:05:11,667 --> 01:05:13,027
Looks like a cancelled stamp.

2084
01:05:13,027 --> 01:05:15,110
(laughs)

2085
01:05:16,707 --> 01:05:19,347
(vocalizes with music)

2086
01:05:19,347 --> 01:05:20,947
- Well time for a drink.

2087
01:05:20,947 --> 01:05:22,347
- Yep, it's getting later and later.

2088
01:05:22,347 --> 01:05:23,707
Tammy?

2089
01:05:23,707 --> 01:05:24,907
I think we'd better take off.

2090
01:05:24,907 --> 01:05:25,907
Ready?

2091
01:05:25,907 --> 01:05:26,909
- Yes, Captain!

2092
01:05:26,909 --> 01:05:27,909
- All right.

2093
01:05:27,909 --> 01:05:29,389
Flyin' high now.

2094
01:05:29,389 --> 01:05:31,189
- You're into what?

2095
01:05:31,189 --> 01:05:32,829
- What? Dan was trapped?

2096
01:05:32,829 --> 01:05:34,549
- Yes, I tried to help him but--

2097
01:05:34,549 --> 01:05:36,589
- He already chewed half his leg off.

2098
01:05:36,589 --> 01:05:38,191
- I heard what he said.

2099
01:05:38,191 --> 01:05:39,711
I can rescue Dan.

2100
01:05:39,711 --> 01:05:41,111
- Can you get in there
before the bomb goes off?

2101
01:05:41,111 --> 01:05:42,111
- I can do that.

2102
01:05:42,111 --> 01:05:43,551
- I can try.

2103
01:05:43,551 --> 01:05:45,311
- We've gotta be sure.

2104
01:05:45,311 --> 01:05:47,471
- We'll never save Dan
by talking about it.

2105
01:05:47,471 --> 01:05:48,671
- Well then let's sing about it!

2106
01:05:48,671 --> 01:05:51,421
- Billy, you stop worrying, okay.

2107
01:05:52,671 --> 01:05:55,231
- Thanks for cheering me up, you're a pip!

2108
01:05:55,231 --> 01:05:56,471
- You guys better get outta here quick.

2109
01:05:56,471 --> 01:05:58,231
Nothing doin', I'm going with you.

2110
01:05:58,231 --> 01:05:59,431
(grunts)

2111
01:05:59,431 --> 01:06:01,031
No, you're not.

2112
01:06:01,031 --> 01:06:03,093
- You get back to the ship.

2113
01:06:03,093 --> 01:06:04,493
- I wanna help you rescue Dan.

2114
01:06:04,493 --> 01:06:05,653
- I wanna know what love is.

2115
01:06:05,653 --> 01:06:06,893
- Your injured leg?

2116
01:06:06,893 --> 01:06:08,733
You'll only be in my way.

2117
01:06:08,733 --> 01:06:11,552
(groans)

2118
01:06:11,552 --> 01:06:12,385
- This is great.

2119
01:06:12,385 --> 01:06:13,617
Do we have to see this?

2120
01:06:13,617 --> 01:06:14,617
Come on.

2121
01:06:14,617 --> 01:06:15,777
- Sounds like he's getting a tattoo

2122
01:06:15,777 --> 01:06:17,577
of the bizzy buzz buzz or something.

2123
01:06:17,577 --> 01:06:20,177
- Oh Victor Kaya, why did
you have to buy the company?

2124
01:06:20,177 --> 01:06:22,897
- What is the nature of your mission here?

2125
01:06:22,897 --> 01:06:24,497
(screams)

2126
01:06:24,497 --> 01:06:26,417
- Shaves like a blade!

2127
01:06:26,417 --> 01:06:29,057
- I'm going to have to drill again.

2128
01:06:29,057 --> 01:06:32,777
- You were collecting
information on our secret weapon.

2129
01:06:32,777 --> 01:06:34,297
You're a spy, aren't you, huh?

2130
01:06:34,297 --> 01:06:36,177
(screaming)

2131
01:06:36,177 --> 01:06:37,179
- Now rinse, please.

2132
01:06:37,179 --> 01:06:38,096
Is it safe?

2133
01:06:39,979 --> 01:06:41,019
(buzzing)

2134
01:06:41,019 --> 01:06:42,779
- Who sent you here?

2135
01:06:42,779 --> 01:06:45,499
- If you don't look
good, we don't look good.

2136
01:06:45,499 --> 01:06:48,339
- Say, you're not enjoying this.

2137
01:06:48,339 --> 01:06:51,019
Now, I think you better answer us.

2138
01:06:51,019 --> 01:06:54,939
Otherwise, things will get even worse!

2139
01:06:54,939 --> 01:06:56,019
(grunts)

2140
01:06:56,019 --> 01:06:57,139
- Just a little off the top!

2141
01:06:57,139 --> 01:06:58,459
- Talk!

2142
01:06:58,459 --> 01:06:59,459
- Talk!

2143
01:06:59,459 --> 01:07:02,579
- Talk talk, by Talk Talk,
from the album talk talk.

2144
01:07:02,579 --> 01:07:04,579
(booms)

2145
01:07:10,819 --> 01:07:13,461
- Yep, thought I could get
Red flying a crop duster

2146
01:07:13,461 --> 01:07:15,381
if I lived long enough.

2147
01:07:15,381 --> 01:07:18,141
(chuckles)

2148
01:07:18,141 --> 01:07:19,981
- Look at that dust.

2149
01:07:19,981 --> 01:07:21,341
- Man, should I be driving?

2150
01:07:21,341 --> 01:07:23,591
I mean, I already got TWIs.

2151
01:07:25,341 --> 01:07:28,091
(dramatic music)

2152
01:07:29,941 --> 01:07:31,461
(gun shots)

2153
01:07:31,461 --> 01:07:32,461
(vocalizes)

2154
01:07:32,461 --> 01:07:34,101
- Interpretive death!

2155
01:07:34,101 --> 01:07:35,261
Flip chop to a somersault!

2156
