- All relative scale.

2419
01:16:50,935 --> 01:16:51,815
- Wait, wait.

2420
01:16:51,815 --> 01:16:53,255
What was the plot here?

2421
01:16:53,255 --> 01:16:54,495
- Plot?

2422
01:16:54,495 --> 01:16:55,737
- Think they blew that up, too.

2423
01:16:55,737 --> 01:16:56,857
(chuckles)

2424
01:16:56,857 --> 01:16:58,737
- It's farfegnugen gone horribly wrong.

2425
01:16:58,737 --> 01:16:59,654
- I'll say.

2426
01:17:01,297 --> 01:17:03,464
(snoring)

2427
01:17:06,459 --> 01:17:08,259
- You know what this reminds me of?

2428
01:17:08,259 --> 01:17:10,339
Thunderbirds, all go!

2429
01:17:10,339 --> 01:17:11,419
(chuckles)

2430
01:17:11,419 --> 01:17:12,619
Remember?

2431
01:17:12,619 --> 01:17:14,786
(crashes)

2432
01:17:18,292 --> 01:17:20,839
- Hey, do they have
another Herb Albert tape?

2433
01:17:20,839 --> 01:17:22,679
I'm really getting sick of this.

2434
01:17:22,679 --> 01:17:23,999
- Eight-track recycled.

2435
01:17:23,999 --> 01:17:27,439
- Oh, that really does look good, though.

2436
01:17:27,439 --> 01:17:28,439
- It looks neat.

2437
01:17:28,439 --> 01:17:30,106
- Pretty impressive.

2438
01:17:35,439 --> 01:17:36,879
- Did Kissinger order this?

2439
01:17:36,879 --> 01:17:37,999
- I think it was Schwarzkopf.

2440
01:17:37,999 --> 01:17:38,832
- Oh.

2441
01:17:42,279 --> 01:17:43,399
- So there's stuff blowing up then.

2442
01:17:43,399 --> 01:17:44,441
- Pretty much.

2443
01:17:44,441 --> 01:17:45,274
- Yup.

2444
01:17:45,274 --> 01:17:47,341
- It's pretty neat.

2445
01:17:47,341 --> 01:17:49,621
- Blowing it up, yupper-doodle-doo.

2446
01:17:49,621 --> 01:17:50,821
- Got some money to blow here.

2447
01:17:50,821 --> 01:17:51,738
- Oh, yeah.

2448
01:17:53,261 --> 01:17:54,461
- This is pretty cool.

2449
01:17:54,461 --> 01:17:55,941
- It does look good, though.

2450
01:17:55,941 --> 01:17:57,781
- Really good.

2451
01:17:57,781 --> 01:17:58,981
- Orgy of destruction.

2452
01:17:58,981 --> 01:18:00,661
- Sorry, everyone!

2453
01:18:00,661 --> 01:18:01,661
Sorry!

2454
01:18:01,661 --> 01:18:03,061
Only meant to blow up that one thing!

2455
01:18:03,061 --> 01:18:04,101
Sorry!

2456
01:18:04,101 --> 01:18:06,263
- It's the Bridge on the
River Kwai over there.

2457
01:18:06,263 --> 01:18:08,513
(whistles)

2458
01:18:14,065 --> 01:18:14,898
- Yup.

2459
01:18:15,745 --> 01:18:17,187
- And they still haven't hit that.

2460
01:18:17,187 --> 01:18:18,437
- Here it goes.

2461
01:18:19,947 --> 01:18:20,947
- Uh oh.

2462
01:18:20,947 --> 01:18:22,707
(booms)

2463
01:18:22,707 --> 01:18:24,290
- Next on MacGyver.

2464
01:18:25,313 --> 01:18:27,829
- Can't begin to tell you
how proud I am of you guys.

2465
01:18:27,829 --> 01:18:28,829
- 'Cause I'm drunk.

2466
01:18:28,829 --> 01:18:31,829
- The greatest crew a Captain ever had.

2467
01:18:31,829 --> 01:18:34,229
(giggles)

2468
01:18:34,229 --> 01:18:35,146
- Hey, Ken!

2469
01:18:36,709 --> 01:18:40,731
- Pull my finger and do
that funny face you do.

2470
01:18:40,731 --> 01:18:41,931
(laughs)

2471
01:18:41,931 --> 01:18:43,764
- Pull my finger, too.

2472
01:18:44,731 --> 01:18:47,731
I love it when they do that.

2473
01:18:47,731 --> 01:18:48,851
- See, it's all working out.

2474
01:18:48,851 --> 01:18:51,813
I wish your mother were here to see this.

2475
01:18:51,813 --> 01:18:53,980
(exhales)

2476
01:18:56,173 --> 01:18:57,333
(yells)

2477
01:18:57,333 --> 01:18:58,413
- So, rangers!

2478
01:18:58,413 --> 01:18:59,933
- Gene Simmons?

2479
01:18:59,933 --> 01:19:01,013
- I'm delighted to report good news.

2480
01:19:01,013 --> 01:19:03,381
Our research center on earth

2481
01:19:03,381 --> 01:19:06,101
has just developed a bomb that
can destroy a whole planet.

2482
01:19:06,101 --> 01:19:08,421
- And you guys can't cut a
simple steak and shrimp combo!

2483
01:19:08,421 --> 01:19:10,141
- We will gain control of that bomb

2484
01:19:10,141 --> 01:19:11,711
and then Valna will dominate the universe!

2485
01:19:11,711 --> 01:19:13,691
- Yes, master.

2486
01:19:13,691 --> 01:19:15,411
- The universe in Wisconsin, Madison,

2487
01:19:15,411 --> 01:19:17,611
a tradition of excellence
for over 200 years.

2488
01:19:17,611 --> 01:19:19,531
- I've been waiting for you, Captain.

2489
01:19:19,531 --> 01:19:20,531
- Five neat guys.

2490
01:19:20,531 --> 01:19:21,891
And a girl.

2491
01:19:21,891 --> 01:19:23,133
- She runs the Reynold's Aluminum plant.

2492
01:19:23,133 --> 01:19:25,053
- It's too dangerous.

2493
01:19:25,053 --> 01:19:26,893
- I'm sorry my father was detained.

2494
01:19:26,893 --> 01:19:27,893
He wanted to welcome you--

2495
01:19:27,893 --> 01:19:28,893
- What?

2496
01:19:28,893 --> 01:19:29,726
- Mother!

2497
01:19:32,415 --> 01:19:33,415
- What's up, Ken?

2498
01:19:33,415 --> 01:19:34,415
- He's tripping.

2499
01:19:34,415 --> 01:19:35,495
- Looked like my mother.

2500
01:19:35,495 --> 01:19:37,055
Why'd she run away?

2501
01:19:37,055 --> 01:19:38,175
- 'Cause she hated kids, maybe?

2502
01:19:38,175 --> 01:19:39,008
- Mother!

2503
01:19:41,015 --> 01:19:42,895
- Hey, not so fast, Ken!

2504
01:19:42,895 --> 01:19:44,735
Take it easy.

2505
01:19:44,735 --> 01:19:46,657
You know you haven't seen
her in several years.

2506
01:19:46,657 --> 01:19:48,537
- Sounds like they're
playing the Godfather theme.

2507
01:19:48,537 --> 01:19:50,617
- But no one every really proved it.

2508
01:19:50,617 --> 01:19:52,057
That's why I--

2509
01:19:52,057 --> 01:19:53,377
- Ken, snap out of it.

2510
01:19:53,377 --> 01:19:54,657
- Come on, this is your mother now.

2511
01:19:54,657 --> 01:19:55,777
Try her out.

2512
01:19:55,777 --> 01:19:58,577
- We've been assigned to
escort this young lady.

2513
01:19:58,577 --> 01:19:59,977
- I beg your pardon.

2514
01:19:59,977 --> 01:20:01,017
- Hi-keeba.

2515
01:20:01,017 --> 01:20:02,737
- That's alright.

2516
01:20:02,737 --> 01:20:04,137
The problem is my father.

2517
01:20:04,137 --> 01:20:05,857
Ever since he developed that bomb,

2518
01:20:05,857 --> 01:20:09,859
all sorts of people have
been threatening me.

2519
01:20:09,859 --> 01:20:10,979
- Look, sir.

2520
01:20:10,979 --> 01:20:13,729
(dramatic music)

2521
01:20:15,019 --> 01:20:19,619
- We're being attacked by
models from Members Only!

2522
01:20:19,619 --> 01:20:20,702
- Take cover!

2523
01:20:22,819 --> 01:20:24,619
- Oh no, it's the Dave Clark Five

2524
01:20:24,619 --> 01:20:28,859
and they're being attacked
by Dino, Dizzy and Billy!

2525
01:20:28,859 --> 01:20:30,739
- It's like one of those Obsession ads.

2526
01:20:30,739 --> 01:20:33,822
If this is love, then find me guilty.

2527
01:20:37,663 --> 01:20:40,005
- Hey, it's the guys from Delta Epsilon!

2528
01:20:40,005 --> 01:20:42,045
- It's the guys from Sigma Fi!

2529
01:20:42,045 --> 01:20:43,965
- This kind of stuff
always happens on campus.

2530
01:20:43,965 --> 01:20:46,567
- Those soldiers move
faster than I expected.

2531
01:20:46,567 --> 01:20:49,085
(grunts)

2532
01:20:49,085 --> 01:20:50,502
- Guido Sarducci?

2533
01:20:51,485 --> 01:20:52,805
- The manufacturer of my invention--

2534
01:20:52,805 --> 01:20:54,165
- Sugar in this gum?

2535
01:20:54,165 --> 01:20:55,605
- Has been preserved on this microfilm--

2536
01:20:55,605 --> 01:20:59,427
- So it doesn't stick to dental work, eh?

2537
01:20:59,427 --> 01:21:00,729
- You mean this little film

2538
01:21:00,729 --> 01:21:02,129
contains information on
a bomb powerful enough

2539
01:21:02,129 --> 01:21:04,129
to blow up the entire universe?

2540
01:21:04,129 --> 01:21:06,089
- No matter what happens to me, Captain,

2541
01:21:06,089 --> 01:21:08,209
this microfilm must not
fall into the wrong hands.

2542
01:21:08,209 --> 01:21:09,369
- Why are they meeting in the shower?

2543
01:21:09,369 --> 01:21:12,011
- My daughter asked me not to
make this invention public.

2544
01:21:12,011 --> 01:21:15,178
- By the way of sitting on the urinal.

2545
01:21:17,131 --> 01:21:18,211
- Tammy's got a Weber Cooker.

2546
01:21:18,211 --> 01:21:19,961
- There she is again!

2547
01:21:23,770 --> 01:21:24,603
- Mother!

2548
01:21:24,603 --> 01:21:26,315
Why does she always run away?

2549
01:21:26,315 --> 01:21:28,715
- Why is she younger than me?

2550
01:21:28,715 --> 01:21:30,355
- Uh oh.

2551
01:21:30,355 --> 01:21:32,035
(dramatic music)

2552
01:21:32,035 --> 01:21:33,075
- Oh man, now he's outside.

2553
01:21:33,075 --> 01:21:36,155
I'd say this part of the
movie needs strict re-writes.

2554
01:21:36,155 --> 01:21:36,988
- A little weird.

2555
01:21:36,988 --> 01:21:38,177
- Hey mom!

2556
01:21:38,177 --> 01:21:40,777
Where'd you get the meadow?

2557
01:21:40,777 --> 01:21:42,817
- We're the catering squad.

2558
01:21:42,817 --> 01:21:44,337
- Hi-keeba.

2559
01:21:44,337 --> 01:21:46,017
- Greetings from our headquarters.

2560
01:21:46,017 --> 01:21:47,497
We have orders to bring you there.

2561
01:21:47,497 --> 01:21:49,497
(gasps)

2562
01:21:50,662 --> 01:21:52,577
- Captain's sportin' a bike rack there.

2563
01:21:52,577 --> 01:21:54,177
(chuckles)

2564
01:21:54,177 --> 01:21:56,057
- Tell your headquarters
they can forget their orders.

2565
01:21:56,057 --> 01:21:56,890
- Captain!

2566
01:21:58,337 --> 01:22:00,920
- Ash Wednesdays, Saysar style.

2567
01:22:02,217 --> 01:22:03,050
- Ouch.

2568
01:22:05,697 --> 01:22:07,539
- Filmed in convolution vision.

2569
01:22:07,539 --> 01:22:08,456
- I'll say.

2570
01:22:09,339 --> 01:22:11,339
(pants)

2571
01:22:18,259 --> 01:22:19,459
- Mother, come back!

2572
01:22:19,459 --> 01:22:21,339
- What in the Sam Scratch is going on?

2573
01:22:21,339 --> 01:22:24,232
- This is an entirely different
movie we're watching here!

2574
01:22:24,232 --> 01:22:25,565
- It was Halkon.

2575
01:22:27,607 --> 01:22:28,687
- Fred Biletnikoff!

2576
01:22:28,687 --> 01:22:29,520
- Attack.

2577
01:22:32,849 --> 01:22:35,849
- Hey, this side shoots to the left!

2578
01:22:41,409 --> 01:22:42,489
- Ken?

2579
01:22:42,489 --> 01:22:43,769
- Where the hell did you come from?

2580
01:22:43,769 --> 01:22:45,529
- All three of them were
to be taken back to Valna.

2581
01:22:45,529 --> 01:22:46,969
- Valna?

2582
01:22:46,969 --> 01:22:48,289
- Get me a spoon.

2583
01:22:48,289 --> 01:22:49,889
- Halkon was going to
hold them as hostages.

2584
01:22:49,889 --> 01:22:51,009
Just a minute.

2585
01:22:51,009 --> 01:22:52,409
This lady can tell you the rest.

2586
01:22:52,409 --> 01:22:53,649
- The rest of the story.

2587
01:22:53,649 --> 01:22:54,929
Page two.

2588
01:22:54,929 --> 01:22:56,209
- Halkon made me do it.

2589
01:22:56,209 --> 01:22:58,449
He wanted me to infiltrate your operation

2590
01:22:58,449 --> 01:23:00,009
posing as Ken's mother.

2591
01:23:00,009 --> 01:23:01,529
- And then he was going to kill her.

2592
01:23:01,529 --> 01:23:03,449
I better pay Halkon a visit.

2593
01:23:03,449 --> 01:23:06,011
(sobs)

2594
01:23:06,011 --> 01:23:07,811
- Ken, you're not going to Valna--

2595
01:23:07,811 --> 01:23:08,851
- Dressed like that.

2596
01:23:08,851 --> 01:23:09,851
- That's crazy.

2597
01:23:09,851 --> 01:23:11,451
- He's right, Ken.

2598
01:23:11,451 --> 01:23:13,091
- What other choice do I have?

2599
01:23:13,091 --> 01:23:14,171
- You could get a smaller belt buckle.

2600
01:23:14,171 --> 01:23:15,491
- Can you people people take on Halkon?

2601
01:23:15,491 --> 01:23:17,091
No way.

2602
01:23:17,091 --> 01:23:18,171
- Jose!

2603
01:23:18,171 --> 01:23:19,491
- It's got to be me.

2604
01:23:19,491 --> 01:23:20,971
- It's just gotta be me!

2605
01:23:20,971 --> 01:23:22,971
- Accept no responsibility,

2606
01:23:22,971 --> 01:23:25,131
you'd be acting on your own, Ken.

2607
01:23:25,131 --> 01:23:26,851
What we can do is wish you good luck.

2608
01:23:26,851 --> 01:23:28,611
- Maybe pack you a few
sandwiches but that's it.

2609
01:23:28,611 --> 01:23:31,491
- He must be destroyed by a Star Wolf!

2610
01:23:31,491 --> 01:23:34,074
- You'll always be a Star Wolf.

2611
01:23:35,171 --> 01:23:36,571
- Never a star.

2612
01:23:36,571 --> 01:23:37,931
(laughs)

2613
01:23:37,931 --> 01:23:39,691
- Is that so awful?

2614
01:23:39,691 --> 01:23:42,093
If I'm able to use my
strength for a good cause?

2615
01:23:42,093 --> 01:23:44,413
- I'm just doing what
Jerry does for those kids!

2616
01:23:44,413 --> 01:23:45,733
- Don't be a fool.

2617
01:23:45,733 --> 01:23:47,653
- Don't be a fool with your life, Billy.

2618
01:23:47,653 --> 01:23:49,693
- Nobody admires you more than I do.

2619
01:23:49,693 --> 01:23:51,813
But you're no match for Halkon.

2620
01:23:51,813 --> 01:23:53,333
- Don't be so sure.

2621
01:23:53,333 --> 01:23:55,173
Halkon trained me for
every sort of combat.

2622
01:23:55,173 --> 01:23:57,413
He taught me well.

2623
01:23:57,413 --> 01:23:58,973
- One thing that Halkon didn't teach you

2624
01:23:58,973 --> 01:24:01,413
was to fight as dirty as he does.

2625
01:24:01,413 --> 01:24:03,373
Which is the reason why,

2626
01:24:03,373 --> 01:24:05,093
you better take some earthlings along.

2627
01:24:05,093 --> 01:24:06,533
- Because we're basically scum.

2628
01:24:06,533 --> 01:24:07,613
(laughs)

2629
01:24:07,613 --> 01:24:08,973
- Exactly what I was thinking.

2630
01:24:08,973 --> 01:24:11,973
(upbeat tech music)

2631
01:24:14,373 --> 01:24:18,675
- I wonder what the king
is drinking tonight.

2632
01:24:18,675 --> 01:24:20,842
(panting)

2633
01:24:22,435 --> 01:24:23,955
- Oh, another Orrin Hatch.

2634
01:24:23,955 --> 01:24:25,235
No, this one's a Richard Hatch.

2635
01:24:25,235 --> 01:24:26,235
- Oh.

2636
01:24:26,235 --> 01:24:28,835
(laughs)

2637
01:24:28,835 --> 01:24:30,275
- One wretched Star Wolf!

2638
01:24:30,275 --> 01:24:33,195
- Two wretched Star Wolves?

2639
01:24:33,195 --> 01:24:34,995
- I don't see any danger in that!

2640
01:24:34,995 --> 01:24:37,578
He had a space escort with him?

2641
01:24:38,835 --> 01:24:40,475
What's become of the others?

2642
01:24:40,475 --> 01:24:44,395
- Well, we tried to locate them, master.

2643
01:24:44,395 --> 01:24:45,395
- He's cute.

2644
01:24:45,395 --> 01:24:46,715
- I want Rockford dead!

2645
01:24:46,715 --> 01:24:48,475
- Every one of them!

2646
01:24:48,475 --> 01:24:50,555
If they're not dead by
nightfall, you'll die!

2647
01:24:50,555 --> 01:24:51,557
- Yes, master!

2648
01:24:51,557 --> 01:24:52,640
- He is cute.

2649
01:24:54,357 --> 01:24:56,832
Kind of looks like Tammy Faye, I think.

2650
01:24:56,832 --> 01:24:58,197
- Star Wolf!

2651
01:24:58,197 --> 01:25:00,447
(exclaims)

2652
01:25:01,652 --> 01:25:03,069
- Looking for me?

2653
01:25:05,953 --> 01:25:07,353
Hello, Star Wolf.

2654
01:25:07,353 --> 01:25:09,155
- Hello, Shirl.

2655
01:25:09,155 --> 01:25:11,975
- Halkon, I promised I'd
return here to settle

2656
01:25:11,975 --> 01:25:13,295
the score.

2657
01:25:13,295 --> 01:25:14,655
- I believe it was 15 love?

2658
01:25:14,655 --> 01:25:15,695
Something like that?

2659
01:25:15,695 --> 01:25:17,535
- Don't move!

2660
01:25:17,535 --> 01:25:20,095
(chuckles)

2661
01:25:20,095 --> 01:25:22,655
- You know you can't
bring yourself to kill me.

2662
01:25:22,655 --> 01:25:24,895
- I'm wearing my magic
rain cape and ski gloves.

2663
01:25:24,895 --> 01:25:28,575
- After all, Star Wolf, I'm
the one who created you.

2664
01:25:28,575 --> 01:25:30,895
Everything you are and everything you know

2665
01:25:30,895 --> 01:25:32,415
you learned from me.

2666
01:25:32,415 --> 01:25:34,255
- Well everything I know
I learned in kindergarten!

2667
01:25:34,255 --> 01:25:36,553
- You haven't the courage
to pull that trigger.

2668
01:25:36,553 --> 01:25:38,575
- You're wrong.

2669
01:25:38,575 --> 01:25:41,735
Everything I learned from you is wrong.

2670
01:25:41,735 --> 01:25:43,015
- Like three card monty.

2671
01:25:43,015 --> 01:25:45,735
- Everything you taught me was evil, evil.

2672
01:25:45,735 --> 01:25:47,135
Now I see another way of life.

2673
01:25:47,135 --> 01:25:48,897
A life that's honest and decent.

2674
01:25:48,897 --> 01:25:49,975
- I'm gonna become a nun!

2675
01:25:49,975 --> 01:25:51,777
- And I've come back to
destroy you and your evil!

2676
01:25:51,777 --> 01:25:52,610
- Ness.

2677
01:25:53,497 --> 01:25:54,617
- Thing.

2678
01:25:54,617 --> 01:25:55,617
- Now die!

2679
01:25:55,617 --> 01:25:56,697
- No, you're the one that's going to die!

2680
01:25:56,697 --> 01:25:57,817
- No, you're the one who's going to die!

2681
01:25:57,817 --> 01:25:59,057
No it's you, no you're
the one who's gonna,

2682
01:25:59,057 --> 01:26:00,390
who's gonna die?

2683
01:26:03,137 --> 01:26:05,337
- Maybe I am gonna die.

2684
01:26:05,337 --> 01:26:06,254
- Hi-keeba.

2685
01:26:09,137 --> 01:26:11,377
